1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:07,591
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,426
[Pani Bottle] Shit, I'm the only survivor.

3
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:13,180
God, I'm so beat.

4
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:23,023
[♪ playful music playing]

5
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:39,331
That's not going to work.

6
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:44,836
Damn, that didn't work.

7
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,713
[exhales]

8
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,299
[sighs frustratedly]

9
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:53,428
Geez, I can't believe this.

10
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:55,639
-[Pani Bottle] Wait, is it over?
-Where were you?

11
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,015
[ZZONE] How did you not get caught?

12
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:58,392
PLAYERS SLOWLY GATHER AFTER INTERROGATIONS

13
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,685
[Joonsu] It's so good to see you.

14
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,561
-Did you find all the clues?
-[ZZONE] What?

15
00:01:01,645 --> 00:01:02,813
-The clues.
-I found three.

16
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,274
[Jimin] It was so hard to find the clues.

17
00:01:05,357 --> 00:01:07,609
-How many clues did you find?
-[ZZONE] Three.

18
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:08,694
How many...

19
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:11,697
-Seriously...
-[Jieun] How many did you find?

20
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,407
-None.
-You're the Madman, aren't you?

21
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:15,450
-[Joonsu] You're the Madman.
-Madman.

22
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:18,495
I swear I'm not.
I just couldn't find them.

23
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:22,624
Jimin said she didn't find a single clue.

24
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:24,793
Not even one?

25
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:26,670
[Jimin] There should be

26
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:29,548
-potential Good Citizens we have in mind.
-I think so. Yes.

27
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:31,091
-[Jimin] Because they're crazy?
-I feel like...

28
00:01:31,592 --> 00:01:33,343
there's one person right now.

29
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:35,262
-[Jimin] Who?
-Something about Yang Dail...

30
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:36,930
-Who do you think he is?
-[Joonsu] It felt off.

31
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:38,015
He did seem a bit suspicious.

32
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:40,100
-[Jaegyun] Why?
-Is he the Madman or a Good Citizen?

33
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:41,810
The Madman. I think he has a special role.

34
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:44,688
It's because he immediately suggested
we all reveal our roles.

35
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:46,732
That actually wasn't a good move.

36
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:48,317
God, I'm freezing to death.

37
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,443
SPEAK OF THE DEVIL

38
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,528
When did you get caught?

39
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:53,363
[Jaegyun] I got caught a little later.

40
00:01:53,447 --> 00:01:56,074
-Good work, everyone.
-Come over here quick.

41
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:57,659
How many clues did you find?

42
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,244
I left everything behind.

43
00:01:59,328 --> 00:02:01,580
-I didn't know we had to keep them.
-[Dail] Wait, then...

44
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,248
You're the Madman, aren't you?

45
00:02:03,332 --> 00:02:05,334
-What?
-You're the Madman, right?

46
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:07,419
-[Horseking] Madman? Me?
-[Dail] Yes. Yes.

47
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:10,464
-The Madman? No, I'm not.
-You aren't the Madman?

48
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:13,383
-[Horseking] This tastes good!
-[Jimin chuckles]

49
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:15,510
If you're not the Madman,
are you a Good Citizen?

50
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:17,095
What? No.

51
00:02:17,179 --> 00:02:19,473
-[Pani Bottle] This is hard.
-[Dail] This is not easy.

52
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:22,392
[Pani Bottle] Did the cops
seem like they'd figured things out,

53
00:02:22,476 --> 00:02:23,518
or did they seem clueless?

54
00:02:23,602 --> 00:02:25,437
-What do you think?
-Somewhere in between?

55
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,689
They were trying to feel me out,
and some were right.

56
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:29,149
THE GOOD CITIZEN'S WHITE LIE

57
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:30,233
So I just said I didn't know.

58
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:32,402
[Jieun] If I were the cops,
it'd be too hard.

59
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:33,487
ROUND 1 COPS MEETING

60
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:36,073
Kim Ddolddol is Burglar 2.

61
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:38,950
-He just admitted that himself.
-What?

62
00:02:39,034 --> 00:02:41,119
What? You think he's a Good Citizen?

63
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,413
Yes, and he also said this.

64
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:44,498
SHARING INTEL FROM DDOLDDOL

65
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:46,667
-"Joonsu's job is a nurse."
-Burglar 3's Joonsu?

66
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,751
PRESUMING BURGLAR 3'S IDENTITY

67
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:50,128
Yes, Burglar 3 is Joonsu.
And I called in Joonsu,

68
00:02:50,212 --> 00:02:51,588
but he didn't say anything.

69
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:54,841
Are you male or female?

70
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:57,427
I'm...

71
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,640
[Sanghyun]
He really seemed like a criminal.

72
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:04,226
COPS' CURRENT SUSPECTS
BURGLAR 2: KIM DDOLDDOL, GOOD CITIZEN

73
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:05,602
BURGLAR 3: LEE JOONSU, CONFIRMED

74
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:08,647
Well, I did have one stroke of luck.

75
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:12,651
The two people I caught...

76
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:13,735
CLUES FROM HORSEKING

77
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:15,278
Here you go.

78
00:03:15,362 --> 00:03:16,363
DECISIVE CLUES

79
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,699
-Casino chips. Casino name tag.
-[Horseking] Yes.

80
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:21,034
CLUES FROM HWANG JAEGYUN

81
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:22,411
[Junseo] A knife sheath.

82
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:23,495
DECISIVE CLUES

83
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:24,663
And a rolling pin.

84
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:27,499
The wooden rolling pin
is a match for these two.

85
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:28,667
-[Sanghyun] I see.
-The rolling pin.

86
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:29,751
CRIMINAL REPORTS

87
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:31,128
[Junseo] It's linked to a drug criminal

88
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:32,212
"DRUG 1, ASSAULT 2
ROLLING PIN"

89
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,755
and an assault criminal.

90
00:03:33,839 --> 00:03:36,299
Of the two who used
a rolling pin in their crimes,

91
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:37,968
one was a casino dealer.

92
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:42,973
And the clues Horseking brought in
were from the casino dealer.

93
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:45,600
So I think Horseking is the casino dealer

94
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:47,144
and Assault Criminal 2.

95
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,437
And Drug Criminal 1?

96
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,230
It's Hwang Jaegyun. I'm 90% sure.

97
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:53,316
Because he's the only one
who has a rolling pin as a weapon.

98
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,693
DRUG CRIMINAL 1
WOODEN ROLLING PIN

99
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:55,777
COPS' CURRENT SUSPECTS

100
00:03:55,861 --> 00:03:59,364
ASSAULT CRIMINAL 2: HORSEKING, LIKELY
DRUG CRIMINAL 1: HWANG JAEGYUN, LIKELY

101
00:03:59,448 --> 00:04:02,367
[Eunsil] By the way, they asked about
which cop roles we had.

102
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:05,120
We can never tell them that.

103
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:08,498
It's because the Madman is trying
to get caught by their assigned cop.

104
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:09,624
[Eunsil] Are there two Madmen?

105
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,084
-It's one, right?
-[Sanghyun] Just one Madman.

106
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,252
THE MADMAN ASKED ABOUT COP ROLES?

107
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,587
Are you with CI?

108
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,880
-[Junseo] CI?
-Or Violent Crimes?

109
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,256
Are you with Narcotics?

110
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:21,094
This makes it too easy
for the cops to figure out.

111
00:04:22,471 --> 00:04:24,848
Get me a bowl of sundae-guk,
I'll spill the beans.

112
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:26,600
Which unit are you from, Detective?

113
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:28,643
Do you want to be arrested?

114
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:31,521
I'd have to be useful
for you to arrest me.

115
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,106
I don't think I'd be much help.

116
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:37,819
ZZONE kept saying "yes" over and over.

117
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,112
-[Sanghyun] ZZONE?
-Yeah.

118
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,364
But she was saying "yes" to everything,

119
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:44,576
so I can't tell if she's a criminal
or a special role.

120
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:46,620
Let's check.

121
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:51,082
All the clues have been revealed.

122
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,878
-[Joonsu] The clues are out.
-[ZZONE] No way.

123
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:57,798
[Jaegyun] They're the clues of criminals
who failed to collect them.

124
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,509
-[Horseking] What's this?
-[Jaegyun] What the heck?

125
00:05:00,592 --> 00:05:02,719
They revealed
three of Pani Bottle's clues.

126
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,890
I found someone else's clue by mistake
and couldn't find my decisive clue.

127
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,850
[Horseking] Ah, by mistake?

128
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:10,769
This is really crucial information.

129
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:12,229
DECISIVE, GENERAL, PENALTY: 1
TOTAL: 3

130
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:15,482
I think he's Assault Criminal 1.

131
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,817
-Pani Bottle.
-[Junseo] Who? Pani Bottle?

132
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,693
ADDRESS: RED LAND
ASSAULT 1 NATIONALITY: RED LAND

133
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:20,445
[Sanghyun] This is a gukbap place
in Red Land.

134
00:05:20,529 --> 00:05:21,655
ASSAULT 1 JOB: TAXI DRIVER

135
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,323
[Eunsil] We found
a taxi driver's car keys too.

136
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,991
[Junseo] Then, this one is confirmed.

137
00:05:25,075 --> 00:05:26,660
ASSAULT 1: PANI BOTTLE, CONFIRMED

138
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:28,703
Don't you think Park Jimin is this one?

139
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:30,288
-Carpenter?
-Doesn't she seem like one?

140
00:05:30,372 --> 00:05:32,123
[Sanghyun] A floor plan and a mask.

141
00:05:32,207 --> 00:05:34,751
-[Eunsil] All clues point to a carpenter.
-[Junseo] Right.

142
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:36,294
-[Sanghyun] It sounds right.
-She's a carpenter.

143
00:05:36,378 --> 00:05:37,462
DRUG 2: PARK JIMIN, CONFIRMED

144
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:38,630
Shin Jieun...

145
00:05:39,631 --> 00:05:41,216
Did we get any clues from her?

146
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:44,010
-We did, but it points to a hairdresser.
-This is confusing.

147
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:45,095
This is driving me crazy.

148
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,889
[Sanghyun] These gloves are used
for cooking too though.

149
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:48,974
[Eunsil] What about the scissors?

150
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,058
JIEUN'S CLUES ARE A BIT ODD

151
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,060
[Junseo] Shin Jieun?

152
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:55,355
Chefs do wear aprons too.

153
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:58,066
-[Sanghyun] Yeah.
-So Shin Jieun could be Burglar 1.

154
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,150
SHIN JIEUN IS BURGLAR 1?

155
00:05:59,234 --> 00:06:01,027
[Sanghyun] Why would Yang Dail have these?

156
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:02,946
Work gloves.

157
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:05,156
[Junseo] Work gloves
belong to someone else.

158
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,908
Work gloves belong to Burglar 1.

159
00:06:06,992 --> 00:06:07,993
DAIL IS BURGLAR 1 TOO?

160
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,911
[Junseo] Right now, we need to verify
Shin Jieun and...

161
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:11,121
"SHIN JIEUN, YANG DAIL
BURGLAR 1"

162
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:12,581
-[Sanghyun] Jieun and Dail.
-[Eunsil] Jieun.

163
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:14,749
[Junseo] Yang Dail.
We're unsure about these two, right?

164
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:16,293
[Sanghyun] We're not sure about them.

165
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:18,879
[Eunsil] There's nothing else
we can guess here.

166
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:21,923
SOMETHING DOESN'T ADD UP

167
00:06:22,007 --> 00:06:23,508
I think we got confused.

168
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:26,511
Shit, I don't think we can arrest them.

169
00:06:28,722 --> 00:06:30,599
We really can't get caught in Round 2.

170
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:32,642
Otherwise, they'll know
who we are for sure.

171
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:34,185
I'm a little scared.

172
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:35,896
[chuckles]

173
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:37,731
It's much better being here.

174
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,274
-[alarm blaring]
-Gosh, that scared me!

175
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:41,276
ROUND 2 CHASE

176
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,903
It's the cleared area!

177
00:06:42,986 --> 00:06:44,404
The cleared area!

178
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,114
[players exclaiming]

179
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:47,616
[Sanghyun] Criminals, get moving.

180
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:49,492
Are you going to B2? [laughing]

181
00:06:49,576 --> 00:06:50,577
Okay, okay.

182
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:51,911
FIND FIVE CLUES AND DON'T GET CAUGHT

183
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,214
PANI BOTTLE GOES THROUGH
SNOW REMOVAL SUPPLY BOX AGAIN

184
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,804
[Pani Bottle] What the heck? It's gone?

185
00:07:10,472 --> 00:07:13,350
I went to the snow removal supply box,
but there was nothing in it.

186
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,060
It made me annoyed.

187
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,269
So I thought about

188
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:19,314
where I'd hide this device
if I were the one who designed it.

189
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:22,275
Since earplugs are small,
I would've stuffed them inside the broom.

190
00:07:22,359 --> 00:07:23,693
But it wasn't in there.

191
00:07:23,777 --> 00:07:24,778
What the fuck?

192
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:29,324
I thought, "Are they messing with me?"
and I looked around.

193
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:32,952
It was wedged between stones.

194
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:35,080
I swear, I wanted to kill whoever hid it.

195
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:37,374
Ah...

196
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,461
I'm finding things so easily.

197
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:47,801
Where did I leave them earlier?

198
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,261
The high heels...

199
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:51,513
Where did I put them?

200
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,848
EARLIER DURING ROUND 1 CHASE

201
00:07:57,060 --> 00:08:00,271
HIGH HEELS

202
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,524
NOW

203
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:05,235
I think I found the high heels
over there earlier.

204
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:08,530
Oh.

205
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:09,739
Where did I put them?

206
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:11,991
I left them here though.

207
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,410
LOOKING IN THE WRONG PLACE

208
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:16,162
Someone must have taken the high heels.

209
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,123
[groans]

210
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:19,749
A MINUTE BEFORE THE COPS ENTER

211
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:21,209
[Pani Bottle] Wait, where am I?

212
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,712
[♪ rock music playing]

213
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:29,217
Are you kidding me? Seriously?

214
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:35,348
God damn it.

215
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:45,525
[host] Cops may enter the chase area.

216
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:46,860
COPS AND ROBBERS ROUND 2

217
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:49,696
HOTEL

218
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,781
POOL

219
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:54,576
THE GROUNDS

220
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:58,830
HORSEKING IS SEARCHING FOR CLUES
IN THE ANNEX

221
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:02,709
QUIET

222
00:09:04,294 --> 00:09:05,462
Okay, I found it.

223
00:09:07,839 --> 00:09:11,885
[Horseking] In Round 1, I was asked
why I didn't bring my clues.

224
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:14,679
Yang Dail started to suspect me for it.

225
00:09:15,764 --> 00:09:18,224
So in Round 2,
I had to find everything no matter what.

226
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:25,899
DECISIVE CLUE

227
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,986
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

228
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:39,788
This isn't it.

229
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:48,546
YUK JUNSEO ENTERS THE ADJACENT ROOM

230
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:57,430
[panting]

231
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:12,445
[both grunting]

232
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:15,365
[exhales]

233
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:33,508
Hold on.

234
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:35,009
[both grunting]

235
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:38,513
Listen.

236
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,268
I'm a Good Citizen.

237
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:44,686
What?

238
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:50,150
[Junseo] All of a sudden,
Horseking said he was a Good Citizen.

239
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,236
-You can believe me later.
-[Junseo] What?

240
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:55,405
-But I need to do my best.
-[Junseo] Yeah.

241
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:56,489
[Horseking panting]

242
00:10:58,366 --> 00:10:59,576
Are you with CI?

243
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,077
-CI?
-Or Violent Crimes?

244
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:04,497
I just have a hunch.

245
00:11:04,581 --> 00:11:07,625
HORSEKING KEPT ASKING ABOUT
YUK JUNSEO'S UNIT

246
00:11:07,709 --> 00:11:09,752
You have to show me your card first.

247
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:14,132
Then, we can reveal our identities
and be allies.

248
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:15,216
Hmm...

249
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:20,305
I don't have to tell you
which unit I'm from

250
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,056
for us to talk, right?

251
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,141
[clicks tongue]

252
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,268
[sighs]

253
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,145
We'll see in Round 2.

254
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,229
All right.

255
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:33,318
[both panting]

256
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:35,361
No, I think you're the Madman.

257
00:11:35,445 --> 00:11:37,989
No, I told you...
If you kill me, only one will be left.

258
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,073
DESPERATE

259
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:41,034
Only one Good Citizen will be left.
I'm helping you.

260
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:42,118
Only I can give you tips.

261
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:44,913
If I catch you now,
it doesn't mean you're dead.

262
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,749
There will be a final vote later anyway.

263
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:48,833
What?

264
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:51,127
-Even if you get caught now--
-I know it's not the end.

265
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:54,589
Yang Dail already suspects me
as the Madman.

266
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,007
He'd ask why I got caught.

267
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:59,427
If I'm caught now,
they'll assume I'm the Madman.

268
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,846
I'd be voted out anyway.

269
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:03,973
I'm trying to make sure I survive

270
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:07,101
and the cops win
by getting rid of the other two criminals.

271
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:08,603
I can't trust this punk.

272
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,563
-I swear, I'm telling the truth.
-What?

273
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:12,440
Look, I don't care if I die, okay?

274
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:13,524
[Horseking] I got a little upset.

275
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:16,611
Just like how a detective
would deal with a criminal,

276
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:18,238
he was talking down to me.

277
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:19,614
No, I think you're the Madman.

278
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:20,823
I can't trust this punk.

279
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:24,869
[Horseking] He kept talking down to me,
but I couldn't afford to get eliminated.

280
00:12:24,953 --> 00:12:27,247
So I pretty much pleaded with him.

281
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,457
I'm going to help you so the cops can win.

282
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,793
What will you do if I spare you?

283
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:34,671
I'll keep sending you updates
about where things are.

284
00:12:34,754 --> 00:12:35,797
I swear, I will.

285
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,550
-To me?
-[Horseking] Yeah.

286
00:12:39,634 --> 00:12:40,635
Right away.

287
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:42,804
So, are we good?

288
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:45,265
I'm not sure.

289
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:48,685
[chuckles] I mean, even if
I'm eliminated now, it's not over for me.

290
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:50,311
Then, I'll trust you this one time.

291
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:52,230
Not just once. Just trust me.

292
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,690
-I'll trust you.
-Yeah.

293
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:55,984
But don't get caught again
or I'll rip off your patch.

294
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,944
Sure, you can rip it off then.

295
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,782
You're not with Narcotics, right?

296
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,867
-You're not my assigned cop, right?
-All right.

297
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:06,786
-You're not my assigned cop?
-What?

298
00:13:07,996 --> 00:13:09,038
Just go on for now.

299
00:13:10,832 --> 00:13:11,958
Here.

300
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,042
[Horseking] Okay.

301
00:13:14,669 --> 00:13:16,004
I'll go the opposite way.

302
00:13:17,547 --> 00:13:18,548
[panting]

303
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,676
[sighs, clears throat]

304
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:24,429
[Junseo] I'm not sure
if I made the right call.

305
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:28,850
[Horseking] I still need to win.

306
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:31,936
[Dail] Stay calm, stay calm.

307
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,062
POOL

308
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:34,147
Here...

309
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:38,401
God damn it, I just need this one.

310
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:39,944
DECISIVE CLUE

311
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:41,946
I just need to find this one thing.

312
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,531
Where is it? [groans]

313
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,867
Stay calm.

314
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:49,787
That was the most crucial clue
that I had to find no matter what.

315
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:52,415
I still remember it.
The victim's scalp photo.

316
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:57,670
I literally swept through the whole area
inch by inch with a broom.

317
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:59,380
I couldn't find that one thing,

318
00:13:59,464 --> 00:14:01,716
so I wasted all my time there.

319
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:05,136
I only need this one thing,
but it's driving me nuts!

320
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:08,097
At least I know it's in this area.

321
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:11,517
COP YOUN SANGHYUN

322
00:14:15,897 --> 00:14:17,190
Hey, Junseo.

323
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:19,233
Junseo, Junseo.

324
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:20,902
Yang Dail is downstairs.

325
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:23,571
He's down by the pool. Let's go together.

326
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,656
[♪ tense music playing]

327
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,335
SPOTS YUK JUNSEO

328
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:42,256
[exclaims]

329
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:49,680
[Sanghyun] He went up!

330
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:09,867
[sighs frustratedly]

331
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:13,788
HWANG JAEGYUN GETS CAUGHT
IN THE MIDDLE OF YANG DAIL'S CHASE

332
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:17,208
JANG EUNSIL JOINS THE CHASE

333
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,719
[Dail] I ran into Jaegyun
while I was running away.

334
00:15:28,803 --> 00:15:32,807
When we were running,
I know for a fact that I went past him.

335
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:37,478
So the detective behind us
should've chased Jaegyun and not me.

336
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:42,775
I was ahead of him,
but when I looked back,

337
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:44,819
Eunsil was chasing me.

338
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:47,321
[panting]

339
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:50,616
YANG DAIL IS OUT OF ENERGY

340
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:54,704
Eunsil is a wrestler,
and she ran a marathon as well.

341
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:02,170
Still, I ran away as much as I could.

342
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:16,309
YANG DAIL HAS DISAPPEARED

343
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:25,484
From what I could see,
Eunsil seemed a little tired.

344
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:27,153
So I thought, "I'm good now."

345
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:33,034
YOUN SANGHYUN SHOWS UP

346
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,661
-God damn it!
-[panting]

347
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,455
[yelling] Stop!

348
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,748
-Stop!
-[patch rips]

349
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:40,833
[exhales aggressively]

350
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,879
[Dail] How come every time
I manage to get away from someone,

351
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:46,714
Sanghyun is always there?

352
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:49,258
I was already drained at that point.

353
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:52,053
I thought, "Why is it him again?"

354
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:54,180
[panting] I'm hungry.

355
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,807
[Sanghyun] I was actually waiting
for the right time.

356
00:16:56,891 --> 00:16:58,976
3 MINUTES AGO

357
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:02,980
BIDING HIS TIME
UNTIL YANG DAIL WORE HIMSELF OUT

358
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:06,234
HOT ON HIS HEELS

359
00:17:06,317 --> 00:17:10,571
Eunsil pretty much wore Dail down,
which is why we were able to catch him.

360
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,782
I was so close!

361
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:15,409
[shouts] This is so annoying.

362
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,995
[host] Tag confirmed.

363
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,622
SANGHYUN TAGS YANG DAIL

364
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:23,209
YANG DAIL

365
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,800
[Joonsu whispering] I'm so damn nervous.

366
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:34,178
Just two more. I only need two more.

367
00:17:34,262 --> 00:17:35,429
POOL

368
00:17:37,265 --> 00:17:40,184
GENERAL CLUES: 2
DECISIVE CLUES: 1

369
00:17:40,268 --> 00:17:41,477
God, this is so scary.

370
00:17:42,937 --> 00:17:47,984
OFF TO FIND THE REMAINING CLUES

371
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:10,256
[Sanghyun] I had this feeling

372
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:13,384
that someone was peeking at me
from behind a pillar.

373
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,678
So I looked over,
and I spotted a silhouette,

374
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,054
and it looked like a man.

375
00:18:17,138 --> 00:18:18,764
But his stomach stuck out a bit,

376
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:22,351
and had slightly hunched shoulders.

377
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:25,021
I knew it had to be Joonsu.

378
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:28,399
He must've thought
that he hadn't been spotted,

379
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,818
so he was still hiding behind the pillar.

380
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:33,112
I figured if I ran, he'd find out.

381
00:18:33,696 --> 00:18:35,948
So I pretended not to notice
and kept walking.

382
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,792
[both laughing]

383
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,378
[grunting]

384
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:55,676
[groans]

385
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,310
[Sanghyun panting]

386
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,189
[Joonsu] I had to make a run for it.

387
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:11,901
I was already caught, but I still ran hard
and went down the stairs.

388
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:17,239
I managed to shake him off,
but then Eunsil showed up out of nowhere.

389
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,284
DROPS CLUE

390
00:19:20,368 --> 00:19:22,119
AFTER DISTRACTING THE COPS

391
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:28,459
[Eunsil] You didn't rip it off?

392
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:31,379
A DESPERATE GETAWAY

393
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:36,133
A COP IS RIGHT ON HIS HEELS

394
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:41,514
JANG EUNSIL IN FRONT

395
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,933
YOUN SANGHYUN IN THE BACK

396
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:49,105
WHILE JANG EUNSIL HOLDS ONTO LEE JOONSU

397
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,189
[patch rips]

398
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,565
[host] Tag confirmed.

399
00:19:51,649 --> 00:19:52,650
SANGHYUN TAGS JOONSU

400
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:53,734
Good job.

401
00:19:53,818 --> 00:19:56,320
[Sanghyun] Eunsil came and helped me
chase him down.

402
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:58,489
I got a lot of help from my fellow cops.

403
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,950
[Eunsil] I was pretty tense
during the first round.

404
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:03,411
But right from the start
of the second round,

405
00:20:03,494 --> 00:20:06,288
I started to get a feel
for where criminals would hide.

406
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:07,665
Geez, you scared me!

407
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:10,292
EUNSIL HAS THE HANG OF IT
AND ARRESTS CONSECUTIVE SUSPECTS

408
00:20:10,376 --> 00:20:11,377
[Ddolddol] Jesus!

409
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:14,672
Wait a second. Detective!

410
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,298
-[chuckling]
-[patch rips]

411
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,925
[host] Tag confirmed.

412
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:19,927
CURRENT ARREST STATUS

413
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:23,013
CI: DAIL, JOONSU,
NARCOTICS: JIMIN, JIEUN, DDOLDDOL

414
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,766
EUNSIL'S PRISON FILLS UP FIRST

415
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:26,851
What the heck?

416
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,519
Did you get caught by Eunsil?
She's so good.

417
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,396
-I'm relieved.
-Why is she so good?

418
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,189
I never thought Eunsil would catch me.

419
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:34,024
She's so sneaky. I didn't hear a thing.

420
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:35,901
I'm a decent runner myself.

421
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:39,238
So, I honestly thought
I wouldn't get caught by Eunsil.

422
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:41,824
[Eunsil] Should we move together?

423
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,117
[Sanghyun] Sure, sure.

424
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,578
HWANG JAEGYUN

425
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:48,289
[Jaegyun] After collecting all five clues,

426
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:51,834
I honestly thought about hiding for a bit.

427
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:54,295
I was running around
looking for a spot to hide,

428
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:56,213
but there was nowhere to hide.

429
00:20:56,297 --> 00:20:58,924
I didn't think I'd fit
in the snow removal supply box.

430
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:01,218
But I was confident
I could shake the cops off,

431
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:02,720
so I just kept walking around.

432
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:11,187
There's one down there. It's Jaegyun.

433
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,898
We need to catch him.
We need to check Jaegyun.

434
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:16,233
There he is.

435
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:20,863
[ZZONE] Hwang!

436
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:21,989
ALL THE COPS TARGET JAEGYUN

437
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:27,953
HWANG JAEGYUN

438
00:21:28,037 --> 00:21:29,330
ZZONE

439
00:21:29,914 --> 00:21:31,874
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

440
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:47,306
[exclaims nervously]

441
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:49,850
[exclaims nervously]

442
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:54,522
ZZONE SPOTTED BY A COP CHASING JAEGYUN

443
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:00,402
Damn it. I was chasing Hwang.

444
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:07,034
[♪ unsettling music playing]

445
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:12,623
QUIET

446
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:20,297
ARE THEY GONE?

447
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:24,844
This is insane.

448
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:27,388
[gasps sharply]

449
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,431
YUK JUNSEO SHOWS UP

450
00:22:35,396 --> 00:22:37,189
JANG EUNSIL WAS HIDING

451
00:22:37,273 --> 00:22:38,941
[ZZONE screams]

452
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:41,694
-Wait a minute. [screams]
-[host] Tag is confirmed.

453
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:42,778
JUNSEO TAGS ZZONE

454
00:22:42,862 --> 00:22:44,864
Hwang Jaegyun ran this way earlier.

455
00:22:44,947 --> 00:22:47,283
-He did? Which way?
-He went outside.

456
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:48,409
He went outside.

457
00:22:50,536 --> 00:22:53,914
ZZONE

458
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:57,626
HOTEL

459
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,379
HWANG JAEGYUN GETS AWAY ONCE AGAIN

460
00:23:15,978 --> 00:23:17,813
YOUN SANGHYUN

461
00:23:20,316 --> 00:23:22,318
[♪ fast-paced music playing]

462
00:23:34,997 --> 00:23:36,415
[footsteps approaching]

463
00:23:50,638 --> 00:23:53,849
[Jaegyun] I knew
I could easily outrun Sanghyun.

464
00:23:53,933 --> 00:23:56,602
I'm confident when it comes to running.

465
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:59,063
He couldn't keep up,
so I was heading to the hotel.

466
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:00,147
JAEGYUN SHAKES OFF SANGHYUN

467
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:02,274
[panting heavily]

468
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:08,614
But then, I saw Jang Eunsil
running in from the front,

469
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:10,658
so I was going to fake her out.

470
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:13,786
Hey!

471
00:24:13,869 --> 00:24:14,870
JAEGYUN SHAKES OFF EUNSIL

472
00:24:14,954 --> 00:24:17,081
[Jaegyun] I faked her out
and ran the other way.

473
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:19,249
[Eunsil] Hey, Yuk Junseo!

474
00:24:19,333 --> 00:24:21,251
YUK JUNSEO WAS HIDING

475
00:24:21,335 --> 00:24:22,753
Hey, Junseo!

476
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:25,798
THREE COPS CLOSE IN TOGETHER

477
00:24:26,757 --> 00:24:28,676
[panting]

478
00:24:29,343 --> 00:24:30,678
-Okay.
-[patch rips]

479
00:24:30,761 --> 00:24:34,640
THE CHASE FINALLY COMES TO AN END

480
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:39,103
HWANG JAEGYUN

481
00:24:40,521 --> 00:24:42,272
[Eunsil] We just need to catch
Pani Bottle.

482
00:24:42,773 --> 00:24:44,066
[Junseo] Pani Bottle.

483
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:54,994
[Eunsil] Hey, Junseo.

484
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,459
Junseo! Hurry and get over here.

485
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:03,544
JUNSEO TAGS PANI BOTTLE

486
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:05,337
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Great work.

487
00:25:05,421 --> 00:25:06,922
[Eunsil] We arrested everyone,

488
00:25:07,006 --> 00:25:09,341
including Pani Bottle,
who got away in Round 1.

489
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:12,344
We really showed teamwork at its best.

490
00:25:12,428 --> 00:25:13,429
Didn't we catch everyone?

491
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:14,763
-Did we get Horseking?
-Horseking.

492
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:16,098
THE LAST REMAINING CRIMINAL: HORSEKING

493
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,895
Please tell me where Horseking is.

494
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:27,317
[phone chimes]

495
00:25:28,110 --> 00:25:29,111
First floor of the hotel.

496
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:31,030
DEADLY TAG
HORSEKING'S LOCATION: HOTEL, 1F

497
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:38,996
[host] The chase is over.

498
00:25:40,831 --> 00:25:42,374
-Good work.
-Good work.

499
00:25:42,458 --> 00:25:43,667
I couldn't find them.

500
00:25:43,751 --> 00:25:45,002
HORSEKING ENTERS THE PRISON

501
00:25:45,085 --> 00:25:46,086
[groans]

502
00:25:47,463 --> 00:25:50,257
I couldn't remember where I put them.

503
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,551
I didn't get a single one.

504
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:54,887
I really tried my best.

505
00:25:56,805 --> 00:25:57,931
[Pani Bottle]
Has everyone been caught now?

506
00:25:58,015 --> 00:26:00,768
-[ZZONE] Yes, I think so.
-[Pani Bottle] That's impressive.

507
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:01,852
This is bad.

508
00:26:03,437 --> 00:26:05,564
I think the cops have already won.

509
00:26:05,647 --> 00:26:08,859
-Yeah, the cops have this one in the bag.
-[Jimin] They're done.

510
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:12,154
-[Sanghyun sighs]
-[Junseo] Should we sit over there?

511
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,741
We should keep analyzing the clues.

512
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:18,368
ROUND 2 COPS MEETING

513
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:21,455
-Earlier, Horseking kept claiming...
-[Sanghyun] Yes?

514
00:26:21,538 --> 00:26:23,707
that he was a good guy.

515
00:26:23,791 --> 00:26:27,127
He promised me he'd help if I let him go.

516
00:26:27,211 --> 00:26:30,923
He said he was going to help me,
but I haven't been able to reach him.

517
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:32,341
-[Sanghyun] Horseking?
-Yeah.

518
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:37,179
Horseking and I had made a deal,
but he didn't follow through.

519
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:39,306
That made me think
he wasn't a Good Citizen

520
00:26:39,389 --> 00:26:41,391
and he was just bluffing.

521
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:43,185
This is so confusing.

522
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:45,312
What's confusing me is...

523
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:47,397
-Yang Dail and Shin Jieun?
-Yang Dail and...

524
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,274
-Yes, Shin Jieun. Those two.
-Who caught Yang Dail?

525
00:26:49,358 --> 00:26:50,400
I did.

526
00:26:50,484 --> 00:26:52,611
The first thing I discovered
when I caught him

527
00:26:53,195 --> 00:26:54,905
was the magic show staff pass.

528
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,115
-[Junseo] The staff pass?
-Yes.

529
00:26:56,198 --> 00:26:57,574
DECISIVE CLUE: MAGIC SHOW STAFF PASS

530
00:26:57,658 --> 00:27:00,577
And another clue was the work gloves.

531
00:27:00,661 --> 00:27:02,830
-[Junseo] I see.
-[Eunsil] Yang Dail...

532
00:27:03,497 --> 00:27:04,665
might be a chef.

533
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:07,084
He wore work gloves
so he wouldn't leave fingerprints

534
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:09,002
and slipped sleeping pills
to a casino guest...

535
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:10,295
"BURGLAR 1 JOB: CHEF"

536
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:11,380
according to the report.

537
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:14,174
But it doesn't add up.
There's no reason why he'd be staff.

538
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:15,551
The magic show staff.

539
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,010
DAIL'S CLUES DON'T MATCH WITH A CHEF

540
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:18,679
Do casinos have magic shows?

541
00:27:19,179 --> 00:27:21,849
[Sanghyun] What confused us
about Yang Dail

542
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:23,183
was the work gloves.

543
00:27:23,934 --> 00:27:28,897
Burglar 1 used work gloves
while committing a robbery.

544
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:31,775
And he had a magic show staff pass.

545
00:27:31,859 --> 00:27:34,319
That makes him the stage director
and Assault Criminal 3.

546
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:36,697
We wondered if Dail was Burglar 1
or Assault Criminal 3.

547
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:40,158
With so many clues,
it was even more confusing.

548
00:27:42,744 --> 00:27:44,037
As for Shin Jieun...

549
00:27:46,248 --> 00:27:47,916
[Sanghyun] What's really strange is,

550
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,127
-isn't this clue way too obvious?
-[Junseo] What?

551
00:27:50,210 --> 00:27:51,670
-The scissors?
-[Sanghyun] Yes.

552
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,755
Did we get any clues from her?

553
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:56,174
-We did, but it points to a hairdresser.
-This is confusing.

554
00:27:56,258 --> 00:27:57,259
This is driving me crazy.

555
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:58,427
ADDITIONAL CLUE FROM JIEUN

556
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:00,053
[Sanghyun]
They're a hairdresser's scissors.

557
00:28:00,137 --> 00:28:01,138
[Eunsil] Shin Jieun.

558
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:04,892
In that case, doesn't that make Shin Jieun
the hairdresser and not Hwang Jaegyun?

559
00:28:04,975 --> 00:28:05,976
DRUG CRIMINAL 1: HAIRDRESSER

560
00:28:06,059 --> 00:28:08,353
Doesn't that clearly
make her the hairdresser?

561
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:12,858
[Sanghyun] I began to suspect
that Shin Jieun was Drug Criminal 1.

562
00:28:12,941 --> 00:28:14,151
DRUG CRIMINAL 1 IS SHIN JIEUN?

563
00:28:14,234 --> 00:28:16,653
You don't have any thoughts
of changing that?

564
00:28:17,154 --> 00:28:19,740
-Hwang Jaegyun...
-[Junseo] I'm pretty certain.

565
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,575
JUNSEO IS SURE JAEGYUN IS DRUG CRIMINAL 1

566
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:25,370
The wooden rolling pin came out
as the exact clue I was looking for.

567
00:28:25,454 --> 00:28:27,164
JAEGYUN'S CLUE: WOODEN ROLLING PIN

568
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:29,333
It says this person threatened others

569
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:32,252
by swinging the rolling pin
while hallucinating.

570
00:28:32,336 --> 00:28:34,212
So I wanted to lock that in.

571
00:28:35,255 --> 00:28:36,757
CONFLICTING GUESSES
ABOUT DRUG SUSPECT 1

572
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:39,968
But hairdressing scissors
aren't really used anywhere else.

573
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:42,429
We have to get everything right.

574
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:46,725
[Eunsil] I was supposed to arrest
the Drug Criminals,

575
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:48,018
but it was so hard to figure out.

576
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:49,394
NARCOTICS COP IN DEEP THOUGHT

577
00:28:49,478 --> 00:28:52,064
[sighs] These two are really confusing.

578
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:55,108
Yeah, I should ask Ddolddol
if he has any information.

579
00:28:55,192 --> 00:28:56,860
I caught Kim Ddolddol.

580
00:28:56,944 --> 00:28:58,737
Okay, that's fine with me.

581
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:03,951
In Round 1, I heard Kim Ddolddol
gave Sanghyun a lot of information,

582
00:29:04,034 --> 00:29:06,411
so I was going to ask him
about the Drug Criminals.

583
00:29:06,495 --> 00:29:07,663
But as soon as he arrived...

584
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:08,747
ROUND 2 INTERROGATION

585
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,958
We have no time, so I'll make it quick.

586
00:29:11,041 --> 00:29:12,376
One thing seems clear.

587
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:14,836
I have a feeling Burglar 1 is Jaegyun.

588
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:18,256
-Why?
-Joonsu and I have made a secret alliance.

589
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,467
Yes, Joonsu?

590
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:22,844
-[Joonsu] Horseking's an Assault Criminal.
-Okay.

591
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:25,722
And I don't think
Jaegyun is someone we can trust.

592
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:28,558
He told someone he's a Burglar
and told others he's an Assault Criminal.

593
00:29:28,642 --> 00:29:33,021
I learned Jaegyun had told someone
that he was a Burglar.

594
00:29:33,105 --> 00:29:35,023
I heard this through several people.

595
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:37,401
Joonsu also told me about it.

596
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:39,653
I think he trusts me completely.

597
00:29:39,736 --> 00:29:42,781
If he's pretending to trust me,
he's smarter than I thought.

598
00:29:42,864 --> 00:29:45,158
But I don't think he's the crafty type.

599
00:29:45,242 --> 00:29:46,284
He's like a simple bear.

600
00:29:46,368 --> 00:29:47,369
KIND OF LIKE A BEAR?

601
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:48,787
I do feel bad though.

602
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:51,415
Isn't it safe to say Jaegyun is a Burglar?

603
00:29:51,498 --> 00:29:53,417
GOOD CITIZEN'S TIP:
JAEGYUN IS A BURGLAR

604
00:29:54,084 --> 00:29:55,127
[Junseo] Show me clues if you have any.

605
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:56,211
THE FOLLOWING INTERROGATION

606
00:29:56,837 --> 00:29:57,879
Glucose candy?

607
00:29:58,714 --> 00:30:00,340
[speaks indistinctly]

608
00:30:02,009 --> 00:30:03,760
-There's a lot.
-Okay.

609
00:30:03,844 --> 00:30:07,305
-Rumors say you're an Assault Criminal.
-I'm just a petty criminal.

610
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:09,182
[Sanghyun] Do you think
Dail is an Assault Criminal?

611
00:30:09,266 --> 00:30:10,851
I'll be straight with you.

612
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:13,228
ROUND 2 INTERROGATION ENDS

613
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:15,731
-[Junseo] Did you get anything useful?
-[Sanghyun] I'm certain now.

614
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:17,232
What confused us was

615
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:20,861
Shin Jieun, Yang Dail, and Hwang Jaegyun.

616
00:30:20,944 --> 00:30:21,945
Based on investigations...

617
00:30:22,029 --> 00:30:24,614
I don't think Jaegyun is a Drug Criminal.

618
00:30:24,698 --> 00:30:26,199
Hwang Jaegyun is Burglar 1.

619
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:27,743
I think you're right.

620
00:30:27,826 --> 00:30:29,453
Shin Jieun could've been Burglar 1.

621
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:30,829
But she's Drug Criminal 1.

622
00:30:30,912 --> 00:30:32,080
She brought a clue.

623
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:34,583
The final clue that convinced me...

624
00:30:35,417 --> 00:30:37,335
was Shin Jieun's debt collection notice.

625
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:40,005
The details said
she had a gambling addiction.

626
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:41,339
DRUG CRIMINAL 1: GAMBLING ADDICTION

627
00:30:41,423 --> 00:30:43,925
There's no doubt she's Drug Criminal 1.

628
00:30:44,009 --> 00:30:45,052
I think we're done.

629
00:30:45,135 --> 00:30:47,345
-[Junseo] Shin Jieun...
-[Sanghyun] But she's Drug Criminal 1.

630
00:30:47,429 --> 00:30:49,639
[Eunsil] Drug Criminal 2 is Park Jimin.

631
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:51,349
Drug Criminal 3 is ZZONE.

632
00:30:52,017 --> 00:30:53,268
[Sanghyun] Burglar 1.

633
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:54,770
Burglar 2 is Kim Ddolddol.

634
00:30:55,562 --> 00:30:57,230
Burglar 3 is Joonsu.

635
00:30:58,023 --> 00:30:59,733
And Pani Bottle is Assault Criminal 1.

636
00:31:00,233 --> 00:31:02,611
-[Eunsil] Horseking is Assault Criminal 2?
-Yes.

637
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:04,488
[Sanghyun] And Yang Dail
is Assault Criminal 3.

638
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:07,032
CRIMINAL PREDICTIONS:
CI, VIOLENT CRIMES, NARCOTICS

639
00:31:07,115 --> 00:31:10,160
[Junseo] We figured out
every criminal's role.

640
00:31:10,243 --> 00:31:14,873
The real question is who among them
are Good Citizens and who is the Madman.

641
00:31:15,874 --> 00:31:17,834
The worst-case scenario is this.

642
00:31:17,918 --> 00:31:20,462
-Arresting the Madman would be a disaster.
-Right.

643
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:21,546
KEY IS TO AVOID HIDDEN MADMAN

644
00:31:23,006 --> 00:31:24,299
Why did she ask me this?

645
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:26,093
She asked if anyone helped us at the end.

646
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:27,177
-[Junseo] Who asked?
-Jieun.

647
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:28,261
[Junseo] What did she ask?

648
00:31:28,345 --> 00:31:31,431
She asked if any of the drug criminals
had tried to help us.

649
00:31:33,767 --> 00:31:35,894
Did you catch all the Drug Criminals?

650
00:31:36,478 --> 00:31:37,813
We're working on it.

651
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,440
Aren't they Jimin and ZZONE?

652
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:43,401
SHIN JIEUN GIVES UP THE DRUG CRIMINALS?

653
00:31:43,485 --> 00:31:44,653
Jimin is...

654
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:47,739
a carpenter.

655
00:31:49,366 --> 00:31:51,743
ZZONE is a bartender.

656
00:31:52,327 --> 00:31:54,704
Are you saying you're a Good Citizen?

657
00:31:56,123 --> 00:31:57,124
Yes, I am.

658
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:00,377
[♪ dramatic music playing]

659
00:32:01,044 --> 00:32:02,546
Among the Drug Criminals...

660
00:32:03,755 --> 00:32:05,382
no one gave you tips, right?

661
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:07,425
-Did anyone help?
-No.

662
00:32:08,593 --> 00:32:10,053
Is it you?

663
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,973
-Yes.
-[Eunsil] All right.

664
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:18,103
[Eunsil] She knows all the women
are Drug Criminals.

665
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:19,563
-I see.
-But then,

666
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:23,733
as she left the room, she asked
if any Drug Criminal tried to help us.

667
00:32:23,817 --> 00:32:25,652
That's why I suspect her.

668
00:32:25,735 --> 00:32:29,322
[Eunsil] There were three people
who claimed they were Good Citizens.

669
00:32:29,406 --> 00:32:31,783
There was no doubt about Kim Ddolddol.

670
00:32:31,867 --> 00:32:33,910
[Eunsil] Are you saying
you're a Good Citizen?

671
00:32:33,994 --> 00:32:34,995
Yes, I am.

672
00:32:35,579 --> 00:32:37,455
I'm a Good Citizen.

673
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:38,999
Only I can give you tips.

674
00:32:40,125 --> 00:32:41,877
[Eunsil] I have no idea who the Madman is.

675
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:42,961
ONE OF THE TWO IS FAKE?

676
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:44,754
[Sanghyun] I really don't know.

677
00:32:45,255 --> 00:32:49,092
I don't think
they would've lied randomly for no reason.

678
00:32:49,176 --> 00:32:50,719
[Junseo] But you never know.

679
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:52,387
We can't say for sure.

680
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:55,348
[Eunsil] Please.

681
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:58,768
This is so hard.
Not just anyone can be a cop.

682
00:32:58,852 --> 00:33:01,563
We should assume
we're going into the Death Match.

683
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,647
[Eunsil] No, no.

684
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:04,608
ROUND 2 PRIVATE TALKS FOR CRIMINALS

685
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:07,110
[Jieun] Let's focus on figuring out
the criminals right now.

686
00:33:07,194 --> 00:33:09,279
We need to find either the Madman
or Good Citizens...

687
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:10,447
[Jieun] The Good Citizens.

688
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:12,199
-We'll be better off.
-We can get away.

689
00:33:12,282 --> 00:33:15,702
[Jimin] Let's identify the Good Citizens
and the Madman.

690
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:18,413
There are two Good Citizens
and one Madman.

691
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:20,665
[ZZONE] We just need to find one
on our own team, right?

692
00:33:20,749 --> 00:33:23,418
[Pani Bottle] For the criminals,
the most important thing

693
00:33:23,501 --> 00:33:25,670
is finding the Good Citizens
or the Madman.

694
00:33:25,754 --> 00:33:27,380
Because even if we're thrown in prison,

695
00:33:27,464 --> 00:33:30,800
as long as we have that information,
criminals can still win.

696
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:32,969
[Dail] I just need
to find the Good Citizen

697
00:33:33,053 --> 00:33:35,138
or Madman on my team to win.

698
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:37,432
CRIMINALS SEARCH FOR THE SPECIAL ROLES

699
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:40,018
I'm sure Ddolddol is Burglar 2.

700
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:48,360
I think Horseking is probably the Madman
because he ended up getting caught.

701
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:50,487
That means he's the Madman.

702
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:51,655
Horseking is the Madman.

703
00:33:51,738 --> 00:33:53,198
DAIL'S ONGOING ACCUSATION OF HORSEKING

704
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:54,950
I've put all the pieces together.

705
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:59,246
From the very beginning,
I was suspicious of Horseking.

706
00:33:59,329 --> 00:34:01,581
[Jimin] Horseking seems like
a regular criminal.

707
00:34:01,665 --> 00:34:03,667
[Jieun] Right, I think Horseking
is just a criminal.

708
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:06,836
[Jimin] He's definitely a criminal.
He was painfully clueless.

709
00:34:07,337 --> 00:34:10,257
I did, but I didn't bring them over.

710
00:34:10,340 --> 00:34:12,425
So you found clues and left them there?

711
00:34:12,509 --> 00:34:14,052
But I don't know where they are.

712
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,136
What are you talking about?

713
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:16,930
[Horseking] Because I didn't
just leave them there.

714
00:34:17,013 --> 00:34:19,557
-Horseking's not the analytical type.
-Exactly.

715
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:22,560
Based on his actions,
Horseking seems like the Madman.

716
00:34:22,644 --> 00:34:25,021
[Pani Bottle] I think
he's just actually crazy.

717
00:34:25,105 --> 00:34:26,356
[laughing]

718
00:34:26,940 --> 00:34:30,068
[Jieun] I can't tell if he's good or not.

719
00:34:30,151 --> 00:34:31,194
[Ddolddol] What do you mean?

720
00:34:31,278 --> 00:34:35,073
[Jieun] I can't tell
if he's a Good Citizen or the Madman.

721
00:34:35,156 --> 00:34:37,701
[Ddolddol] What did
the Drug Criminal team think?

722
00:34:37,784 --> 00:34:42,914
[Jieun] I don't think ZZONE is a criminal.

723
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:44,582
[Jimin] The criminal?

724
00:34:44,666 --> 00:34:45,667
From the Drug Criminal team.

725
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,252
SHIN JIEUN IS SUSPICIOUS OF ZZONE

726
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:51,589
I started having doubts about ZZONE
because before Round 1...

727
00:34:51,673 --> 00:34:52,674
BEFORE ROUND 1

728
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:54,301
What if I trip and fall outside?

729
00:34:54,968 --> 00:34:56,094
[players laughing]

730
00:34:56,177 --> 00:35:00,056
[Jimin] She was putting so much effort
into finding clues.

731
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:03,059
When I saw that,
I didn't suspect her at all.

732
00:35:03,143 --> 00:35:05,854
I thought she was working so hard
because she's a criminal.

733
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:07,897
I think they're a criminal,

734
00:35:07,981 --> 00:35:11,860
because some other people didn't make
much of an effort to search for clues.

735
00:35:11,943 --> 00:35:13,028
[gasps]

736
00:35:13,737 --> 00:35:15,905
Right. That's so smart.

737
00:35:18,033 --> 00:35:19,451
[Jimin] She said, "That's so smart."

738
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:22,120
She said the same thing to me.

739
00:35:22,203 --> 00:35:24,497
-Something felt off to me.
-She likes to flatter...

740
00:35:24,581 --> 00:35:25,749
SHIN JIEUN AGREES WITH PARK JIMIN

741
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:28,001
She also suddenly said to me,
"You're so smart."

742
00:35:28,084 --> 00:35:29,961
At that moment, something felt off.

743
00:35:30,045 --> 00:35:33,131
[Jimin] So, I also think she's either
the Madman or the other.

744
00:35:33,214 --> 00:35:35,216
One of the two, but I just can't tell.

745
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:37,927
Now that you've heard what I said,
what do you think?

746
00:35:39,304 --> 00:35:42,057
[Jieun sighs] I don't know.

747
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:48,355
[Ddolddol] I think if there's anyone
pushing hard to accuse someone else,

748
00:35:48,438 --> 00:35:50,815
we should be suspicious of that person.

749
00:35:53,860 --> 00:35:56,738
Once someone else is framed,
it takes the heat off themselves.

750
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:58,073
[mic feedback]

751
00:35:58,156 --> 00:36:00,492
[host] Interrogation time is over.

752
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:04,204
We will reveal the clues
of criminals who failed to retrieve them.

753
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,373
[sighs] It's going to reveal everything.

754
00:36:06,456 --> 00:36:08,416
[sighs] I'm doomed.

755
00:36:08,500 --> 00:36:10,210
-I'm done for.
-You won't see mine.

756
00:36:10,293 --> 00:36:11,795
-Must be nice.
-We won't?

757
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:13,296
[Jaegyun] Yes, I found all five.

758
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:14,547
-Really?
-What? Really?

759
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:16,841
[Joonsu] No way.
You found four already earlier.

760
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:19,469
-I found all four earlier.
-No way! Is he the Madman?

761
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:21,262
Madman? I worked hard and found them all.

762
00:36:21,346 --> 00:36:23,848
-I did my best.
-[Joonsu] I think you tried too hard.

763
00:36:23,932 --> 00:36:25,600
[Jaegyun] I just did my best. But why?

764
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:28,144
[Ddolddol] They all suddenly started
to accuse Jaegyun as the Madman.

765
00:36:28,228 --> 00:36:29,229
I got lucky.

766
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:31,231
BURGLAR TEAM

767
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:32,857
[Jaegyun] Why is it so confusing?

768
00:36:32,941 --> 00:36:35,902
Jaegyun's the only one
without any clues revealed.

769
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:37,278
KIM DDOLDDOL FUELS THE SUSPICION

770
00:36:37,362 --> 00:36:39,989
And the fact that he found
all the clues twice doesn't add up.

771
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,326
[Dail] You're torn
between the two right now.

772
00:36:43,993 --> 00:36:45,662
[Joonsu] He's more likely
to be a Good Citizen.

773
00:36:45,745 --> 00:36:47,831
-It's more likely.
-[Ddolddol] Yeah, since there are two.

774
00:36:47,914 --> 00:36:49,290
If we make that call,

775
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:51,126
-we should assume he's a Good Citizen.
-Right.

776
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,210
VENTRILOQUISM

777
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:54,713
Jaegyun has to be a Good Citizen.

778
00:36:54,796 --> 00:36:56,089
[clears throat]

779
00:36:56,172 --> 00:36:58,633
[Ddolddol] Joonsu trusted me completely.

780
00:36:58,717 --> 00:36:59,718
AS IF CONFLICTED

781
00:36:59,801 --> 00:37:02,512
He's either the Madman
or a Good Citizen. It's fifty-fifty.

782
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:04,389
[Joonsu] He's more likely
to be a Good Citizen.

783
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:06,224
-It's more likely.
-Yeah, since there are two.

784
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:09,811
So, I'm going with Jaegyun
as a Good Citizen.

785
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:11,730
AS IF HE FOUND IT CONVINCING

786
00:37:11,813 --> 00:37:13,064
That's the best option.

787
00:37:13,148 --> 00:37:14,816
This is going so smoothly for me.

788
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:15,900
[chuckles]

789
00:37:16,443 --> 00:37:18,611
MEANWHILE, THE DRUG CRIMINAL TEAM

790
00:37:18,695 --> 00:37:20,280
Who do you think is the Madman?

791
00:37:24,659 --> 00:37:26,703
[gasps] What do you think?

792
00:37:27,871 --> 00:37:31,708
[Dail] Make the right choices.

793
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:33,293
Come over here.

794
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:35,670
Don't let some strange scheme...

795
00:37:35,754 --> 00:37:36,755
[Jieun hesitates]

796
00:37:37,839 --> 00:37:40,049
-I'm sure about ZZONE.
-[Jimin] Right.

797
00:37:40,133 --> 00:37:42,385
I'm sure about ZZONE, because right now,

798
00:37:42,469 --> 00:37:44,262
-she can't lie.
-[Jimin] I'm not sure.

799
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:50,018
The most important thing
is I tried feeling out Eunsil.

800
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,186
[Jimin] Okay.

801
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,604
On the Drug Criminal team,

802
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:56,232
there has to be either
a Good Citizen or the Madman.

803
00:37:56,316 --> 00:37:59,819
It has to be ZZONE.

804
00:37:59,903 --> 00:38:01,946
Jieun was really aggressive about it.

805
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:06,409
She was so determined to convince me.
Her eyes were opening up so wide.

806
00:38:06,493 --> 00:38:08,119
She was right up in my face.

807
00:38:08,203 --> 00:38:10,163
-Just this once, please trust me.
-[Jimin] Okay.

808
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:11,873
Trust me this once.

809
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:13,166
[Jimin sighs]

810
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:16,085
[Jieun] Whether I'm right or wrong,
just look at the odds.

811
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:20,423
Is everyone done with the interrogations?

812
00:38:20,507 --> 00:38:22,926
-Yes.
-Do you think they know everything?

813
00:38:23,009 --> 00:38:26,638
-I feel the cops know everything.
-Honestly, I felt like they don't know.

814
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:30,016
-They knew who was which number.
-I think they'll get everything right.

815
00:38:30,099 --> 00:38:31,601
They'll get everything right.

816
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,728
They seemed unsure though.

817
00:38:34,687 --> 00:38:37,106
So, let me explain it to you.

818
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:39,818
They seemed unsure to you,

819
00:38:40,652 --> 00:38:43,071
because you were definitely
not a criminal.

820
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:46,282
-What does that mean?
-You're a Good Citizen or the Madman.

821
00:38:46,366 --> 00:38:49,410
-That's what they thought?
-[Dail] That's why they seemed unsure.

822
00:38:49,494 --> 00:38:51,120
No, it's not me.

823
00:38:51,204 --> 00:38:52,747
[Horseking] Seriously, Yang Dail

824
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:55,959
kept accusing me from the very beginning.

825
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:59,671
He looked like a madman when he said,
"You're the Madman, aren't you?"

826
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:00,922
That's how he was,

827
00:39:02,215 --> 00:39:03,424
so I was really annoyed.

828
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:06,135
I don't believe this guy. It's not true.

829
00:39:06,219 --> 00:39:07,262
ASSAULT CRIMINAL TEAM

830
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:08,847
-Wait.
-I'm sure.

831
00:39:08,930 --> 00:39:11,474
PANI BOTTLE TAKES JAEGYUN SOMEWHERE

832
00:39:11,558 --> 00:39:12,976
-[Pani Bottle] Really?
-[Jaegyun] Yes.

833
00:39:13,059 --> 00:39:15,395
Which one of the two do you think it is?

834
00:39:15,478 --> 00:39:17,897
-[Jaegyun] Who?
-Between Dail and Horseking.

835
00:39:17,981 --> 00:39:20,066
I just wanted to trust Dail,

836
00:39:20,149 --> 00:39:22,026
-so I thought it was Horseking.
-[Pani Bottle] Right.

837
00:39:22,610 --> 00:39:24,362
But I really don't know right now.

838
00:39:25,113 --> 00:39:26,531
-Well, no one does.
-Right.

839
00:39:29,576 --> 00:39:32,829
We need to discuss altogether anyway.

840
00:39:32,912 --> 00:39:34,289
-Right.
-We do.

841
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,124
Well, the main issue is

842
00:39:36,207 --> 00:39:39,252
we don't know who the Good Citizens
and the Madman are here.

843
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:41,004
We need to decide who's a Good Citizen...

844
00:39:41,921 --> 00:39:44,048
-And who's the Madman.
-...and who's the Madman.

845
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:46,009
We need to decide that.

846
00:39:46,676 --> 00:39:48,595
[♪ mysterious music playing]

847
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:56,477
-[Pani Bottle] Can we talk for a moment?
-[Jaegyun] Wait. This is so sudden. Geez.

848
00:39:56,561 --> 00:39:59,689
Wait, why do you keep having
private conversations?

849
00:39:59,772 --> 00:40:00,773
You're not on the same team.

850
00:40:01,900 --> 00:40:03,693
It's because we're not on the same team.

851
00:40:03,776 --> 00:40:05,904
I don't get it.
We need to look on our own teams...

852
00:40:05,987 --> 00:40:06,988
YANG DAIL GETS IRRITATED

853
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:09,741
It's because we all have
shared information.

854
00:40:09,824 --> 00:40:11,910
[Dail] This is throwing me off.

855
00:40:12,452 --> 00:40:14,203
They're confusing me at the very end.

856
00:40:14,287 --> 00:40:18,166
[Dail] It was almost time to vote,
but he chose to talk to someone else

857
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:20,376
instead of me.

858
00:40:20,460 --> 00:40:22,128
How do you think that makes me feel?

859
00:40:22,712 --> 00:40:23,880
"What's this?"

860
00:40:24,464 --> 00:40:27,091
"This guy is suspecting me."

861
00:40:27,675 --> 00:40:30,261
[Pani Bottle] We wanted
to ask you something too.

862
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:32,680
Did Horseking really try
to show you his card?

863
00:40:32,764 --> 00:40:34,223
-[Jaegyun] Yeah.
-Did he show you or try to?

864
00:40:34,307 --> 00:40:36,309
He tried to show it, but I stopped him.

865
00:40:36,392 --> 00:40:38,478
ROUND 1 PRISON

866
00:40:38,561 --> 00:40:40,104
You're not supposed to show it.

867
00:40:40,188 --> 00:40:43,066
HORSEKING ALMOST SHOWED HIS PROFILE CARD

868
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:46,903
[Pani Bottle] Damn, I'm completely lost.
I feel like it's fifty-fifty right now.

869
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:49,030
-It's driving me crazy.
-I know. [sighs]

870
00:40:50,573 --> 00:40:52,158
[Pani Bottle] This is driving me crazy.

871
00:40:52,742 --> 00:40:53,993
[sighs deeply]

872
00:40:54,077 --> 00:40:55,119
-What?
-[Jaegyun] Nothing.

873
00:40:55,203 --> 00:40:57,246
[Pani Bottle] I mean, it's odd.
No matter how clueless one is,

874
00:40:57,330 --> 00:41:01,042
if people see "Good Citizen" on your card,
that would be a disaster.

875
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:02,335
Yet he tried to show it?

876
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:03,670
When I heard that,

877
00:41:03,753 --> 00:41:06,464
I started thinking,
"Maybe he's not the traitor."

878
00:41:06,547 --> 00:41:09,676
From that point on,
since he'd been making aggressive claims,

879
00:41:09,759 --> 00:41:11,344
I started suspecting Dail.

880
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:12,679
He seemed a bit strange.

881
00:41:12,762 --> 00:41:14,639
He was getting worked up

882
00:41:14,722 --> 00:41:17,684
and started to make me slowly think,
"Is he the Madman?"

883
00:41:18,851 --> 00:41:20,186
[sighs deeply]

884
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,273
They made this God damn game well.

885
00:41:26,776 --> 00:41:28,152
Can I talk to Horseking first?

886
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:29,237
-Sure.
-Yes.

887
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:30,446
[Horseking] About what?

888
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:35,076
-Seriously, why is this confusing you?
-[Joonsu] Listen...

889
00:41:35,159 --> 00:41:36,452
[sighs]

890
00:41:37,245 --> 00:41:40,039
Either way, we have to pick
one of two people.

891
00:41:40,748 --> 00:41:43,793
-I just need to decide that.
-To me, it seems like...

892
00:41:47,338 --> 00:41:49,048
[whispers] Yang Dail is the Madman.

893
00:41:49,132 --> 00:41:51,092
[♪ tense music playing]

894
00:41:51,968 --> 00:41:55,763
I hate to say this,
but I'm suspicious of you too.

895
00:41:55,847 --> 00:41:56,848
I can't really...

896
00:41:56,931 --> 00:41:59,892
If you can't even trust me,
we're out of options.

897
00:41:59,976 --> 00:42:02,854
I'm going to vote for Dail as the Madman.

898
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:04,188
We have to go with that.

899
00:42:04,272 --> 00:42:05,732
I see. I get it.

900
00:42:05,815 --> 00:42:06,899
Okay, okay.

901
00:42:07,984 --> 00:42:09,318
Dail.

902
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:10,903
Dail.

903
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:13,906
Shouldn't the two of us talk?

904
00:42:13,990 --> 00:42:15,491
Dail, have a talk with me too.

905
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:17,994
No, let's all talk together.

906
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:19,412
[Pani Bottle]
We'll talk after you two finish.

907
00:42:19,495 --> 00:42:22,290
-No, let's talk together.
-[Pani Bottle] What's the point of that?

908
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:24,375
-It's someone among us three.
-But I think...

909
00:42:24,459 --> 00:42:25,460
VOICES GRADUALLY GET LOUDER

910
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:28,421
-I think we can talk together.
-[Pani Bottle] I'll let you talk first.

911
00:42:29,130 --> 00:42:31,799
Dail kept insisting
that the three of us should talk.

912
00:42:31,883 --> 00:42:34,260
But I wanted to talk one-on-one.

913
00:42:34,343 --> 00:42:37,055
You have to talk one-on-one
to understand what's going on.

914
00:42:37,138 --> 00:42:40,099
But he kept saying
the three of us should talk together.

915
00:42:40,183 --> 00:42:41,809
That felt even more suspicious.

916
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:43,519
Here's the thing.

917
00:42:43,603 --> 00:42:47,065
From the very beginning,
I trusted Pani Bottle completely.

918
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:52,445
But toward the end,
I felt like I made a mistake.

919
00:42:53,029 --> 00:42:54,113
What's going on?

920
00:42:55,615 --> 00:42:59,911
That's not it. Anyhow, I think...

921
00:42:59,994 --> 00:43:02,205
It's so easy to get this one right.

922
00:43:06,167 --> 00:43:07,877
[Pani Bottle] I need
to listen to them first.

923
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:12,090
[sighs] This is hard.

924
00:43:14,842 --> 00:43:16,010
[Dail] Guys, I'm...

925
00:43:16,094 --> 00:43:17,720
-Guys, I'm going to vote.
-[Pani Bottle] Okay.

926
00:43:17,804 --> 00:43:19,347
-Right now?
-Wait...

927
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:22,934
YANG DAIL SUDDENLY GOES TO CAST HIS VOTE

928
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:24,268
[sighs]

929
00:43:28,356 --> 00:43:31,317
[dealer] Hello.
Please vote to identify the traitor.

930
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,485
VIOLENT CRIMES BURGLAR

931
00:43:32,568 --> 00:43:34,487
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

932
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:37,949
-[sighs] This isn't it.
-[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle.

933
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:41,953
Write down the person you suspect
with a special role.

934
00:43:43,913 --> 00:43:45,373
[Horseking] I chose Yang Dail.

935
00:43:46,499 --> 00:43:47,959
-Hello.
-[dealer] Hello, Kim Ddolddol.

936
00:43:48,042 --> 00:43:49,043
GOOD CITIZEN KIM DDOLDDOL

937
00:43:49,127 --> 00:43:50,378
[Ddolddol] I hope
the detectives get it right.

938
00:43:50,461 --> 00:43:51,462
CI TEAM
GOOD CITIZEN: JAEGYUN

939
00:43:52,380 --> 00:43:57,093
[Ddolddol] Joonsu has complete faith in me
so I'm not worried at all.

940
00:43:57,176 --> 00:43:58,344
Please, please, please.

941
00:43:59,262 --> 00:44:02,348
[Jimin] It's possible that Jieun
was just really good at acting.

942
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:03,599
Maybe she tricked me?

943
00:44:04,892 --> 00:44:06,018
Seriously...

944
00:44:10,022 --> 00:44:12,775
[♪ suspenseful music intensifies]

945
00:44:14,152 --> 00:44:17,822
[host] The Main Match,
"Cops and Robbers," has ended.

946
00:44:19,157 --> 00:44:21,868
All players,
please gather in the Main Hall.

947
00:44:24,871 --> 00:44:25,872
[sighs]

948
00:44:29,417 --> 00:44:31,085
I can't trust anyone now.

949
00:44:31,169 --> 00:44:33,671
-[Jieun] Oh, my God. I want to go home.
-[Dail] I can't trust anyone.

950
00:44:33,754 --> 00:44:37,216
[host] It's time to reveal
the identities of all the players.

951
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:41,470
COPS MUST IDENTIFY
THE CRIMINALS' TRUE IDENTITIES

952
00:44:41,554 --> 00:44:43,764
BURGLAR 1, 2, 3
ASSAULT 1, 2, 3, DRUG 1, 2, 3

953
00:44:43,848 --> 00:44:46,267
JAEGYUN, DDOLDDOL, JOONSU
PANI BOTTLE, HORSEKING, DAIL

954
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:48,603
JIEUN, JIMIN, ZZONE

955
00:44:49,312 --> 00:44:50,313
We got it.

956
00:44:51,063 --> 00:44:52,064
We got it right.

957
00:44:52,148 --> 00:44:55,193
ASIDE FROM THE SPECIAL ROLES,
THEY GUESSED THE CRIMINALS CORRECTLY

958
00:44:55,276 --> 00:44:57,153
[gasps] The cops got it right.

959
00:44:58,613 --> 00:45:01,407
THE ONLY MYSTERY LEFT IS THE SPECIAL ROLES

960
00:45:01,991 --> 00:45:05,953
[host] Among the criminals,
the first Good Citizen is...

961
00:45:06,037 --> 00:45:08,414
[♪ tense music playing]

962
00:45:09,081 --> 00:45:10,791
[Jimin] It was really confusing.

963
00:45:13,294 --> 00:45:15,046
[Ddolddol] I was confident
I wouldn't be caught.

964
00:45:15,963 --> 00:45:18,257
[host] The first Good Citizen is...

965
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:19,842
Kim Ddolddol.

966
00:45:19,926 --> 00:45:21,510
FIRST GOOD CITIZEN IS KIM DDOLDDOL

967
00:45:21,594 --> 00:45:25,097
CI TEAM'S ASSIGNED TRAITOR: BURGLAR 2

968
00:45:25,181 --> 00:45:27,391
CI TEAM'S ASSIGNED TRAITOR: KIM DDOLDDOL

969
00:45:27,475 --> 00:45:28,476
What?

970
00:45:30,019 --> 00:45:32,021
[♪ dramatic music playing]

971
00:45:34,649 --> 00:45:36,567
We were doomed from Round 1.

972
00:45:38,569 --> 00:45:39,612
[groans]

973
00:45:39,695 --> 00:45:42,949
Ddolddol. Ddolddol!

974
00:45:43,032 --> 00:45:44,325
I'm sorry.

975
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:47,245
I trusted him so much.

976
00:45:48,204 --> 00:45:51,123
[Joonsu] My biggest mistake
was trusting Ddolddol too much.

977
00:45:51,207 --> 00:45:55,795
That's when I realized it.
"Right. This is a survival game."

978
00:45:55,878 --> 00:45:57,338
Everyone is my enemy.

979
00:45:58,256 --> 00:46:01,884
I'm definitely going to get back
at Ddolddol and betray him.

980
00:46:01,968 --> 00:46:03,261
I can't just sit back and take it.

981
00:46:04,929 --> 00:46:08,266
[host] We will reveal
the second Good Citizen.

982
00:46:09,016 --> 00:46:12,395
LAST GOOD CITIZEN CANDIDATE
IS FROM VIOLENT CRIMES OR NARCOTICS

983
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:17,775
The Good Citizen is...

984
00:46:18,651 --> 00:46:19,652
ASSAULT CRIMINAL 2

985
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:20,778
THE GOOD CITIZEN

986
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:21,988
Horseking.

987
00:46:23,322 --> 00:46:24,657
[groans]

988
00:46:25,992 --> 00:46:26,993
It was Horseking.

989
00:46:29,495 --> 00:46:30,997
[gasps]

990
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:32,081
[Pani Bottle gasps]

991
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,710
[dealer] You are Assault Criminal 2.

992
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:38,004
Also, you are a Good Citizen.

993
00:46:38,087 --> 00:46:39,839
[gasps] Me?

994
00:46:40,381 --> 00:46:44,427
My strategy was
to not play the role as a Good Citizen.

995
00:46:44,510 --> 00:46:46,554
I was going to act like a regular criminal

996
00:46:46,637 --> 00:46:49,640
to fool both the cops and the criminals.

997
00:46:49,724 --> 00:46:52,310
-I don't have a map.
-[Jimin] Didn't you see the clues?

998
00:46:52,393 --> 00:46:53,394
Hey, they're all in here.

999
00:46:53,477 --> 00:46:54,478
PRETENDING TO NOT UNDERSTAND

1000
00:46:54,562 --> 00:46:56,022
I acted as if I was clueless.

1001
00:46:56,105 --> 00:46:58,190
I pretended I couldn't do anything.

1002
00:46:58,274 --> 00:47:00,943
And as a criminal on the run,
I did my best.

1003
00:47:01,027 --> 00:47:03,696
But I also decided to get physical
and get my hands dirty.

1004
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:06,198
ROUND 1 CHASE

1005
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:10,536
ROUND 2 CHASE

1006
00:47:10,619 --> 00:47:13,956
I didn't want to be suspected
as a Good Citizen.

1007
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:15,624
Jaegyun said he saw it.

1008
00:47:16,459 --> 00:47:18,794
I think that kind of helped.

1009
00:47:18,878 --> 00:47:22,423
Didn't Jaegyun say
he saw me on the ground?

1010
00:47:22,506 --> 00:47:23,841
USING JAEGYUN'S WITNESS ACCOUNT

1011
00:47:23,924 --> 00:47:26,302
Then, Jaegyun gave the tip.

1012
00:47:26,385 --> 00:47:29,847
As for the Drug Criminal team,
it's likely Jieun and Jimin.

1013
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:31,682
You think Dail is an Assault Criminal?

1014
00:47:31,766 --> 00:47:34,602
He told me he's an Assault Criminal,
and he's Assault Criminal 3.

1015
00:47:34,685 --> 00:47:38,439
[Horseking] I shared some helpful intel
based on what I knew.

1016
00:47:38,522 --> 00:47:39,857
I gave them tips.

1017
00:47:43,611 --> 00:47:44,612
Seriously...

1018
00:47:45,821 --> 00:47:48,032
[Dail] I'm such an idiot.

1019
00:47:48,115 --> 00:47:51,077
If I had stuck to my guns
and written Horseking at the end,

1020
00:47:51,160 --> 00:47:53,162
I wouldn't have felt this dumb afterward.

1021
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:57,541
I ended up voting for Pani Bottle,
so I feel like even more of an idiot.

1022
00:47:59,502 --> 00:48:00,878
VIOLENT CRIMES
GOOD CITIZEN: PANI BOTTLE

1023
00:48:00,961 --> 00:48:02,254
TRAITOR VOTE
DAIL CHOSE PANI BOTTLE

1024
00:48:02,338 --> 00:48:03,547
Why is he suspecting me?

1025
00:48:03,631 --> 00:48:07,301
At first, I couldn't understand it.

1026
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:10,513
I thought it was ridiculous.
Then, I got thrown off.

1027
00:48:10,596 --> 00:48:12,181
"Wait a minute."

1028
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:15,267
Does that mean
when Horseking was acting clueless,

1029
00:48:15,351 --> 00:48:16,727
it was actually real...

1030
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:19,688
and was Pani Bottle lying
from the beginning?

1031
00:48:19,772 --> 00:48:22,400
I shouldn't have let it happen,
but I wavered.

1032
00:48:23,526 --> 00:48:25,111
[groans, clicks tongue]

1033
00:48:25,194 --> 00:48:27,113
[Pani Bottle] Where did it all go wrong?

1034
00:48:27,196 --> 00:48:29,448
I realized I'd made the wrong choice.

1035
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:34,078
CI TEAM
GOOD CITIZEN: YANG DAIL

1036
00:48:34,829 --> 00:48:37,623
TRAITOR VOTE
PANI BOTTLE CHOSE DAIL

1037
00:48:39,125 --> 00:48:41,335
-Horseking was so good.
-But now...

1038
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:44,463
[host] And finally,
we will reveal the Madman.

1039
00:48:45,214 --> 00:48:48,509
ALL THAT REMAINS IS TO CATCH THE MADMAN
FROM THE DRUG CRIMINALS TEAM

1040
00:48:49,510 --> 00:48:52,138
[Jimin] I didn't suspect Jieun at all.

1041
00:48:55,683 --> 00:48:57,852
[host] On the Drug Criminal team,
the Madman is...

1042
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:02,857
Drug Criminal 3, ZZONE is the Madman.

1043
00:49:04,316 --> 00:49:06,819
DRUG CRIMINALS IDENTIFY THE MADMAN

1044
00:49:06,902 --> 00:49:08,946
[both chuckle]

1045
00:49:09,029 --> 00:49:11,073
I told you to trust me.

1046
00:49:13,117 --> 00:49:15,161
[Jieun] It was my own strategy.

1047
00:49:15,244 --> 00:49:20,249
I actually had no idea if ZZONE
was a Good Citizen or the Madman.

1048
00:49:20,332 --> 00:49:21,709
In the interrogation room...

1049
00:49:21,792 --> 00:49:23,961
Did you catch all the Drug Criminals?

1050
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:26,172
Aren't they Jimin and ZZONE?

1051
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:31,510
I pretended to be a Good Citizen
to see how they'd react.

1052
00:49:31,594 --> 00:49:32,970
Among the Drug Criminals...

1053
00:49:34,263 --> 00:49:36,015
no one gave you tips, right?

1054
00:49:36,098 --> 00:49:37,099
No.

1055
00:49:37,725 --> 00:49:38,726
Is it you?

1056
00:49:39,685 --> 00:49:43,147
A Good Citizen's role is to help the cops.

1057
00:49:44,023 --> 00:49:45,024
But there was no one.

1058
00:49:45,107 --> 00:49:46,108
So, the answer is clear.

1059
00:49:46,734 --> 00:49:49,445
The Madman is definitely on our team.

1060
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:52,281
[ZZONE] I was disappointed.

1061
00:49:53,073 --> 00:49:56,035
I'm supposed to pretend to be a criminal.

1062
00:49:56,994 --> 00:49:59,163
[groans] I'm going nuts.

1063
00:49:59,955 --> 00:50:01,624
How do I pull off the Madman?

1064
00:50:02,333 --> 00:50:03,709
Looking back,

1065
00:50:03,792 --> 00:50:08,464
things could have turned out differently
if I had acted a little smarter.

1066
00:50:09,048 --> 00:50:11,300
[host] The Narcotics cop...

1067
00:50:11,884 --> 00:50:15,054
Why did she ask me this?
She asked if anyone helped us at the end.

1068
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:18,140
Jieun thought there was a Good Citizen
among the Drug Criminals.

1069
00:50:18,224 --> 00:50:20,684
-She was trying to find them.
-[Eunsil] Okay.

1070
00:50:20,768 --> 00:50:22,061
[Sanghyun]
Because she's not a Good Citizen.

1071
00:50:22,144 --> 00:50:24,230
-She's a criminal.
-She's a criminal.

1072
00:50:24,313 --> 00:50:26,106
I think that's why. It's not her.

1073
00:50:26,190 --> 00:50:27,399
SANGHYUN IDENTIFIED JIEUN'S INTENT

1074
00:50:27,483 --> 00:50:28,484
It's not Jieun.

1075
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:30,319
[Eunsil] When I talked to Jimin,

1076
00:50:30,402 --> 00:50:33,072
it seemed like
she didn't want to get arrested.

1077
00:50:33,572 --> 00:50:36,325
That made me think
she's just a regular criminal.

1078
00:50:36,909 --> 00:50:39,203
ZZONE might be the Madman.

1079
00:50:40,037 --> 00:50:42,581
[host] The Narcotics cop
successfully caught the criminal.

1080
00:50:42,665 --> 00:50:43,791
JIEUN AND JIMIN ARE ARRESTED

1081
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:47,378
[Eunsil] It felt so good. I felt so proud.

1082
00:50:47,461 --> 00:50:49,129
NARCOTICS UNIT
JIEUN, JIMIN, ZZONE

1083
00:50:49,213 --> 00:50:51,966
SUCCESSFULLY CAPTURED THE MADMAN

1084
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:56,262
[host] In Deadly Tag's first match,
"Cops and Robbers,"

1085
00:50:56,345 --> 00:50:57,471
the winners are...

1086
00:50:58,556 --> 00:50:59,682
Youn Sanghyun...

1087
00:51:00,266 --> 00:51:01,350
Yuk Junseo...

1088
00:51:01,892 --> 00:51:02,935
Jang Eunsil...

1089
00:51:03,894 --> 00:51:04,895
[all gasp]

1090
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:07,773
ALL THREE COPS SUCCEEDED

1091
00:51:07,856 --> 00:51:09,149
[host] Shin Jieun...

1092
00:51:09,817 --> 00:51:11,277
Kim Ddolddol...

1093
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:12,486
[player gasps]

1094
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:13,779
Horseking...

1095
00:51:13,862 --> 00:51:14,863
[players exclaim]

1096
00:51:14,947 --> 00:51:15,948
and Park Jimin.

1097
00:51:16,031 --> 00:51:17,032
FOUR CRIMINALS SUCCEEDED

1098
00:51:17,116 --> 00:51:19,118
-Nice, nice.
-Where's Horseking?

1099
00:51:20,327 --> 00:51:21,954
He was unbelievable.

1100
00:51:22,037 --> 00:51:23,038
[Horseking] It felt great.

1101
00:51:23,122 --> 00:51:26,333
If I keep this momentum up,
I might be able to win.

1102
00:51:26,417 --> 00:51:27,543
Like this.

1103
00:51:27,626 --> 00:51:29,169
I want to dance like this.

1104
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:30,254
VICTORY DANCE

1105
00:51:30,337 --> 00:51:34,133
But I thought I'd look uncool,
so I quietly sat back down.

1106
00:51:35,301 --> 00:51:37,886
[host] Winners, please take
your prize money of 20 million won

1107
00:51:37,970 --> 00:51:39,888
and your Elimination Immunity Passes.

1108
00:51:40,431 --> 00:51:43,726
[dealer] Here is your 20 million won
and Elimination Immunity Pass.

1109
00:51:44,351 --> 00:51:47,980
Your 20 million won
will be kept in your personal locker.

1110
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:51,233
It was a perfect day today.

1111
00:51:51,317 --> 00:51:53,235
[host] And the losers are...

1112
00:51:54,236 --> 00:51:55,487
Hwang Jaegyun...

1113
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:57,406
Lee Joonsu...

1114
00:51:58,449 --> 00:51:59,450
Pani Bottle...

1115
00:52:00,367 --> 00:52:01,368
Yang Dail...

1116
00:52:02,703 --> 00:52:04,330
and ZZONE.

1117
00:52:04,413 --> 00:52:05,414
[Dail sighs]

1118
00:52:05,497 --> 00:52:07,166
All I can do is sigh.

1119
00:52:08,709 --> 00:52:11,045
[Pani Bottle] I feel like
I lost so helplessly.

1120
00:52:11,128 --> 00:52:14,590
The disappointment and defeat
all came crashing down on me.

1121
00:52:15,883 --> 00:52:17,092
[host] In Deadly Tag,

1122
00:52:17,176 --> 00:52:19,762
elimination candidates
will be decided through a vote.

1123
00:52:19,845 --> 00:52:22,473
Players without
Elimination Immunity Passes

1124
00:52:22,556 --> 00:52:24,433
are subject to the Elimination Vote.

1125
00:52:25,059 --> 00:52:26,268
All players,

1126
00:52:26,352 --> 00:52:29,104
please choose two players
to send to the Death Match

1127
00:52:29,688 --> 00:52:31,357
and cast your vote.

1128
00:52:31,940 --> 00:52:35,152
Additional votes cost 20 million won each.

1129
00:52:35,235 --> 00:52:38,489
This transaction is only available
in the Dealer Room during voting time.

1130
00:52:38,572 --> 00:52:41,909
Also, players may transfer funds
between each other,

1131
00:52:41,992 --> 00:52:45,704
but all transactions must take place
in the presence of a Dealer.

1132
00:52:45,788 --> 00:52:48,457
Voting will close in an hour.

1133
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:51,835
VOTING BEGINS

1134
00:52:51,919 --> 00:52:54,963
[timer beeping]

1135
00:52:56,048 --> 00:52:58,550
[players chattering indistinctly]

1136
00:53:00,052 --> 00:53:04,181
-I showed everything to you, Pani Bottle.
-I know.

1137
00:53:04,264 --> 00:53:06,433
I do admit that I got confused.

1138
00:53:06,517 --> 00:53:09,645
But when you picked me,
I had no other choice.

1139
00:53:09,728 --> 00:53:10,729
-[Dail] Right.
-Isn't that true?

1140
00:53:10,813 --> 00:53:13,399
But this is what I thought.

1141
00:53:13,482 --> 00:53:15,943
You completely ignored me.

1142
00:53:16,026 --> 00:53:17,945
But that's actually not true.

1143
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:20,072
I said I wanted to talk to you at the end.

1144
00:53:21,240 --> 00:53:25,077
I needed to talk with people,
so I called whoever was nearby.

1145
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:28,122
I was going to talk to you,
but you suddenly wouldn't talk to me.

1146
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:32,501
That's because we talked first
from the very beginning.

1147
00:53:32,584 --> 00:53:33,836
Then, the order should be--

1148
00:53:33,919 --> 00:53:36,004
Honestly, the order doesn't matter.

1149
00:53:36,088 --> 00:53:37,214
That's how I saw it.

1150
00:53:37,297 --> 00:53:40,926
You became suspicious of me
even though I'd been honest with you.

1151
00:53:41,009 --> 00:53:43,721
Then, everything I thought I knew
about you started to change.

1152
00:53:43,804 --> 00:53:45,764
Well, it's easy to say so in hindsight.

1153
00:53:46,932 --> 00:53:50,811
[sighs] I handed him everything,
but Pani Bottle didn't utilize it at all,

1154
00:53:50,894 --> 00:53:52,229
and I felt so frustrated.

1155
00:53:52,312 --> 00:53:54,189
It made my blood boil.

1156
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:56,024
[sighs]

1157
00:53:58,819 --> 00:54:01,238
Dail, let's work together
to get the Immunity Pass.

1158
00:54:03,949 --> 00:54:05,242
We need to survive this.

1159
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:08,287
[Joonsu] I just needed to survive this.

1160
00:54:10,789 --> 00:54:12,291
Horseking, let's go talk.

1161
00:54:13,041 --> 00:54:14,460
A SUDDEN REQUEST TO TALK

1162
00:54:14,543 --> 00:54:16,003
Why all of a sudden?

1163
00:54:16,086 --> 00:54:19,214
Is this how it usually goes?
We always have to go off and talk?

1164
00:54:19,298 --> 00:54:20,424
JOONSU TAKES ACTION FIRST

1165
00:54:20,507 --> 00:54:23,427
You have to help me this time.
Please help me.

1166
00:54:24,011 --> 00:54:25,137
I'm so scared.

1167
00:54:26,388 --> 00:54:29,141
I won't vote you out,
because I promised to help you.

1168
00:54:29,850 --> 00:54:31,226
For real.

1169
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:34,772
ASKS WITH AN INNOCENT SMILE

1170
00:54:34,855 --> 00:54:36,648
Please help me out just this once.

1171
00:54:36,732 --> 00:54:37,941
I really need your help.

1172
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:39,985
Thank you.

1173
00:54:41,278 --> 00:54:42,863
[Joonsu] Since I'm the youngest,

1174
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:46,992
I'm kind of in a position
where I get a lot of love.

1175
00:54:47,075 --> 00:54:48,577
I always smile when I talk.

1176
00:54:53,874 --> 00:54:56,460
It looks like Joonsu
is going around buying votes.

1177
00:54:56,543 --> 00:54:58,295
-[Jaegyun] I know.
-Should I do something too?

1178
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:00,923
Geez.

1179
00:55:01,006 --> 00:55:02,716
OTHER ELIMINATION CANDIDATES GET MOVING

1180
00:55:03,342 --> 00:55:05,177
Eunsil, you know, right?

1181
00:55:05,802 --> 00:55:07,721
We don't attack our allies.

1182
00:55:07,804 --> 00:55:10,098
[all chuckle]

1183
00:55:10,182 --> 00:55:12,893
[Eunsil] Since I'm friends with Dail,

1184
00:55:12,976 --> 00:55:15,062
I wasn't thinking about voting for him.

1185
00:55:15,145 --> 00:55:17,189
Junseo, you know, right?

1186
00:55:17,272 --> 00:55:19,358
I helped you from the very beginning.

1187
00:55:19,441 --> 00:55:22,069
BRIEF BUT BIG HELP

1188
00:55:22,653 --> 00:55:24,404
-Remember?
-Yes, I do.

1189
00:55:24,488 --> 00:55:25,781
-Ddolddol.
-Yes?

1190
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:27,407
You tricked me, Ddolddol.

1191
00:55:27,991 --> 00:55:30,369
Ddolddol, you tricked me once.
You can't do it twice.

1192
00:55:31,787 --> 00:55:32,788
[exclaims]

1193
00:55:33,497 --> 00:55:36,750
[ZZONE] It felt a little embarrassing
to ask directly,

1194
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:38,335
but I couldn't get eliminated.

1195
00:55:39,253 --> 00:55:42,631
-Please don't pick me. Help me out.
-Sure, I don't think you will.

1196
00:55:43,298 --> 00:55:44,591
Please help me out.

1197
00:55:45,259 --> 00:55:46,593
-For real...
-[Sanghyun] Why?

1198
00:55:47,553 --> 00:55:48,845
-Why?
-[ZZONE] Why?

1199
00:55:54,268 --> 00:55:55,269
[Dail whispers] Joonsu.

1200
00:56:00,399 --> 00:56:02,234
Let's vote her out.

1201
00:56:02,317 --> 00:56:04,528
-Okay.
-Let's vote ZZONE out.

1202
00:56:04,611 --> 00:56:05,988
PLOTTING TO ELIMINATE ZZONE

1203
00:56:07,239 --> 00:56:10,325
So, we know one person will be ZZONE.

1204
00:56:10,409 --> 00:56:12,786
And Pani Bottle told us to vote him out.

1205
00:56:12,869 --> 00:56:15,205
PANI BOTTLE GAVE UP?

1206
00:56:15,289 --> 00:56:16,832
[sighs deeply]

1207
00:56:18,041 --> 00:56:19,209
[Pani Bottle] I'll go.

1208
00:56:19,293 --> 00:56:20,669
-What?
-[Pani Bottle] I'll go.

1209
00:56:20,752 --> 00:56:22,504
[Pani Bottle] I don't deserve to be here.

1210
00:56:22,588 --> 00:56:24,881
Personally, I felt quite defeated.

1211
00:56:24,965 --> 00:56:27,759
I was determined
not to go through that defeat again.

1212
00:56:27,843 --> 00:56:31,138
I felt like going into the Death Match,
winning it, and surviving

1213
00:56:31,221 --> 00:56:33,307
was the only way to overcome this.

1214
00:56:33,390 --> 00:56:36,393
I'll get voted out.
And you vote for one more person.

1215
00:56:36,476 --> 00:56:37,477
That's not right.

1216
00:56:37,561 --> 00:56:38,562
TRYING TO STOP PANI BOTTLE

1217
00:56:38,645 --> 00:56:40,689
No, don't do that.
Let's leave it to the vote.

1218
00:56:40,772 --> 00:56:42,149
You did nothing wrong.

1219
00:56:42,232 --> 00:56:44,401
-[ZZONE] Exactly.
-[Pani Bottle] I did. But anyway...

1220
00:56:46,361 --> 00:56:49,489
Then, we'll vote for Pani Bottle
and ZZONE.

1221
00:56:49,573 --> 00:56:53,535
Or we could each buy one extra vote
and vote for those people.

1222
00:56:53,619 --> 00:56:55,871
[Joonsu] You want to buy one to be safe?

1223
00:56:55,954 --> 00:56:56,997
We could do that.

1224
00:56:57,497 --> 00:57:00,417
-Then, that's two votes for each of us.
-That's right.

1225
00:57:00,500 --> 00:57:02,669
PROMISE TO BUY EXTRA VOTES
TO PICK ZZONE & PANI BOTTLE

1226
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:05,672
-Let's stick together and not lie.
-Sure. I don't lie.

1227
00:57:05,756 --> 00:57:07,132
You really won't lie to me?

1228
00:57:07,215 --> 00:57:09,635
I told Joonsu we'd spend our money

1229
00:57:09,718 --> 00:57:13,013
to each buy an extra vote
to vote out ZZONE.

1230
00:57:13,096 --> 00:57:15,766
Pani Bottle volunteered to go
to the Death Match,

1231
00:57:15,849 --> 00:57:17,976
and he wanted us to vote him out.

1232
00:57:18,060 --> 00:57:19,519
He wanted to get voted out...

1233
00:57:20,729 --> 00:57:23,440
So I mean, there's no reason not to.

1234
00:57:23,523 --> 00:57:25,317
[Jaegyun sighs] I don't know what to do.

1235
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:28,028
[Dail] We have no choice
but to vote for Pani Bottle.

1236
00:57:30,030 --> 00:57:31,198
Let's go to the back.

1237
00:57:34,868 --> 00:57:36,328
[Jaegyun] Who else do you want to pick?

1238
00:57:37,037 --> 00:57:38,997
-There's no other option.
-ZZONE?

1239
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,000
[Dail] That's what Joonsu and I agreed on.

1240
00:57:42,084 --> 00:57:43,377
Okay.

1241
00:57:43,460 --> 00:57:47,130
Dail suggested we all vote for one person.

1242
00:57:47,214 --> 00:57:49,383
I got promises from Jaegyun and Joonsu,

1243
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:51,551
so we'd each spend 20 million won
to each have two votes.

1244
00:57:51,635 --> 00:57:53,428
[dealer] Would you like
to buy extra votes?

1245
00:57:53,512 --> 00:57:54,513
Yes.

1246
00:57:54,596 --> 00:57:56,139
There's nothing I can do.

1247
00:57:56,223 --> 00:57:57,808
PANI BOTTLE

1248
00:57:57,891 --> 00:57:59,518
ZZONE

1249
00:57:59,601 --> 00:58:02,604
-An additional vote costs 20 million won.
-Okay.

1250
00:58:02,688 --> 00:58:06,942
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE
PANI BOTTLE, ZZONE

1251
00:58:09,444 --> 00:58:10,445
What will you do?

1252
00:58:11,363 --> 00:58:12,948
The safe bet would be

1253
00:58:13,657 --> 00:58:17,786
someone who's good at survival games
and likely to last a long time.

1254
00:58:17,869 --> 00:58:18,870
Right.

1255
00:58:18,954 --> 00:58:20,580
HORSEKING THINKS THE STRONG
SHOULD BE GONE

1256
00:58:20,664 --> 00:58:21,665
Junseo.

1257
00:58:23,375 --> 00:58:26,795
Do you think we should vote out
people who are good at games?

1258
00:58:28,463 --> 00:58:29,506
For me...

1259
00:58:31,091 --> 00:58:32,968
I see it differently.

1260
00:58:33,593 --> 00:58:34,594
If you trap someone,

1261
00:58:35,137 --> 00:58:37,681
they might have no choice
but to strike back

1262
00:58:38,348 --> 00:58:39,850
at the opposing side.

1263
00:58:40,642 --> 00:58:41,643
That's why.

1264
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:44,896
The idea of eliminating
the strongest player

1265
00:58:44,980 --> 00:58:46,732
feels a bit one-dimensional.

1266
00:58:50,110 --> 00:58:51,862
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE
PANI BOTTLE, ZZONE

1267
00:58:51,945 --> 00:58:54,156
YUK JUNSEO PICKED ZZONE

1268
00:58:54,239 --> 00:58:56,742
CURRENT VOTING TOTALS
PANI BOTTLE 5 VOTES, DAIL 0 VOTES

1269
00:58:56,825 --> 00:58:59,161
ZZONE 5 VOTES
JAEGYUN 0 VOTES, JOONSU 0 VOTES

1270
00:58:59,244 --> 00:59:02,164
[sighs] Should I buy extra votes or not?

1271
00:59:04,791 --> 00:59:06,084
DAIL, JAEGYUN

1272
00:59:06,168 --> 00:59:09,755
ZZONE VOTED FOR YANG DAIL
AND HWANG JAEGYUN

1273
00:59:22,976 --> 00:59:24,686
This is so heartbreaking.

1274
00:59:26,438 --> 00:59:27,689
There's nothing I can do.

1275
00:59:30,942 --> 00:59:32,736
[host] Voting has closed.

1276
00:59:33,445 --> 00:59:35,197
We will announce the results.

1277
00:59:35,739 --> 00:59:38,283
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1278
00:59:38,867 --> 00:59:40,368
Here are the voting results.

1279
00:59:40,452 --> 00:59:43,121
The player with the most votes is...

1280
00:59:44,956 --> 00:59:45,999
Pani Bottle.

1281
00:59:47,793 --> 00:59:49,252
[Pani Bottle] Just as I expected.

1282
00:59:49,961 --> 00:59:51,963
[host] The next
Death Match candidate is...

1283
00:59:58,136 --> 00:59:59,679
Yang Dail.

1284
00:59:59,763 --> 01:00:01,890
[gasps]

1285
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:06,436
[♪ dramatic music playing]

1286
01:00:09,189 --> 01:00:10,649
[Dail] I couldn't believe it.

1287
01:00:10,732 --> 01:00:12,317
It was unbelievable.

1288
01:00:12,400 --> 01:00:15,028
If Joonsu and Jaegyun
had kept their promises,

1289
01:00:15,111 --> 01:00:18,031
I likely wouldn't have been picked.

1290
01:00:18,114 --> 01:00:20,158
One of these bastards broke their promise.

1291
01:00:20,242 --> 01:00:25,288
As I realized that, I thought,
"You can't trust these damn people."

1292
01:00:25,372 --> 01:00:28,250
RESULTS
PANI BOTTLE 12 VOTES, DAIL 7 VOTES

1293
01:00:28,333 --> 01:00:31,169
ZZONE 5 VOTES,
JAEGYUN 4 VOTES, JOONSU 0 VOTES

1294
01:00:33,004 --> 01:00:34,005
That's a relief.

1295
01:00:34,673 --> 01:00:36,049
[Joonsu] I think everything was...

1296
01:00:37,300 --> 01:00:39,302
thanks to Jimin.

1297
01:00:39,386 --> 01:00:42,180
30 MINUTES AGO

1298
01:00:42,264 --> 01:00:45,183
Can you come here for a moment?
I have something to tell you.

1299
01:00:45,851 --> 01:00:47,519
One vote costs 20 million won.

1300
01:00:48,186 --> 01:00:51,064
If you give us 10 million won each,
that's two votes.

1301
01:00:51,147 --> 01:00:53,775
ASKING FOR 10 MILLION WON PER PERSON
IN EXCHANGE FOR HELP

1302
01:00:53,859 --> 01:00:56,069
But if I say no, you're going to pick me.

1303
01:00:56,152 --> 01:00:57,737
This isn't right.

1304
01:00:57,821 --> 01:00:58,822
Just don't vote for me.

1305
01:00:58,905 --> 01:00:59,906
DAIL REJECTS JIMIN'S OFFER

1306
01:00:59,990 --> 01:01:00,991
I'm begging you.

1307
01:01:01,074 --> 01:01:03,577
Well, that's...

1308
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:05,954
It's not easy to buy two votes
with 10 million won.

1309
01:01:06,037 --> 01:01:08,331
But Dail wouldn't trust me.

1310
01:01:09,457 --> 01:01:10,625
From that point on,

1311
01:01:10,709 --> 01:01:12,836
I thought it'd be better
if he got eliminated.

1312
01:01:13,461 --> 01:01:15,171
Can you help me out just one time?

1313
01:01:15,255 --> 01:01:16,923
JOONSU APPROACHES WITH A SMILE

1314
01:01:17,007 --> 01:01:19,801
[Jimin] Joonsu slowly came over

1315
01:01:19,885 --> 01:01:21,761
and asked me not to vote him out.

1316
01:01:21,845 --> 01:01:24,764
But I couldn't do it for free.
We just met.

1317
01:01:25,724 --> 01:01:30,478
Then, if you give me and Jieun
10 million won each,

1318
01:01:30,562 --> 01:01:31,980
you can get two votes

1319
01:01:32,063 --> 01:01:34,274
for the price of one.

1320
01:01:34,357 --> 01:01:35,358
IMMEDIATELY ACCEPTS

1321
01:01:35,442 --> 01:01:37,235
-Okay, I'll ask.
-Okay. Thank you.

1322
01:01:40,530 --> 01:01:43,033
I needed someone on my side
who I could trust.

1323
01:01:43,116 --> 01:01:45,702
Jieun and I had built a bond

1324
01:01:45,785 --> 01:01:47,662
from winning together.

1325
01:01:47,746 --> 01:01:48,747
This was good news.

1326
01:01:48,830 --> 01:01:53,543
If Joonsu gives Jieun and me
10 million won each to vote,

1327
01:01:53,627 --> 01:01:57,380
it's good for Joonsu, me, and Jieun.

1328
01:01:57,464 --> 01:01:59,215
Three birds, one stone, right?

1329
01:01:59,299 --> 01:02:01,593
And Joonsu can't be eliminated.

1330
01:02:01,676 --> 01:02:03,553
He is such a useful asset.

1331
01:02:03,637 --> 01:02:04,888
[inhales sharply]

1332
01:02:04,971 --> 01:02:06,598
I wanted to keep him around.

1333
01:02:06,681 --> 01:02:09,434
[dealer] You have transferred
10 million won to Shin Jieun.

1334
01:02:09,517 --> 01:02:11,603
-To Park Jimin...
-10 million won.

1335
01:02:11,686 --> 01:02:13,355
-Yes, 10 million won.
-[dealer] 10 million won.

1336
01:02:13,438 --> 01:02:15,357
Rather than paying
20 million won for one vote,

1337
01:02:15,440 --> 01:02:18,735
giving 10 million won each
would be a win-win for both sides.

1338
01:02:20,820 --> 01:02:22,489
PANI BOTTLE
DAIL

1339
01:02:22,572 --> 01:02:25,617
[Jimin] I picked Pani Bottle
and the one who turned down my offer.

1340
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:27,118
Yang Dail.

1341
01:02:27,202 --> 01:02:31,039
And when taking off the belt earlier,
ZZONE helped me.

1342
01:02:31,122 --> 01:02:33,875
I wanted to at least
do something to help her.

1343
01:02:34,459 --> 01:02:39,714
[Jimin] The one who may be difficult
to compete against later on is Dail.

1344
01:02:39,798 --> 01:02:41,508
Okay. Dail and...

1345
01:02:44,511 --> 01:02:47,514
[Joonsu] At first, I was going to pick
ZZONE and Pani Bottle,

1346
01:02:47,597 --> 01:02:50,100
but Jimin told me to pick Yang Dail

1347
01:02:50,183 --> 01:02:51,309
because he's strong.

1348
01:02:51,393 --> 01:02:52,560
So I thought,

1349
01:02:52,644 --> 01:02:55,605
"Well, as long as it's not me
and as long as I survive, it's okay."

1350
01:02:55,689 --> 01:02:56,690
So I picked him.

1351
01:02:56,773 --> 01:02:58,483
ENDS UP BETRAYING DAIL

1352
01:02:59,192 --> 01:03:00,443
There's nothing I can do.

1353
01:03:01,695 --> 01:03:03,780
[Jimin] It was a great plan.

1354
01:03:03,863 --> 01:03:05,031
EVERYTHING GOES AS SHE HAD PLANNED

1355
01:03:05,115 --> 01:03:07,951
[host] Yang Dail and Pani Bottle,

1356
01:03:09,285 --> 01:03:11,788
please exit the Main Hall immediately.

1357
01:03:13,123 --> 01:03:15,250
-Win and come back to us.
-[laughs]

1358
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:16,751
Go out there and win.

1359
01:03:18,795 --> 01:03:21,381
It wasn't me. Seriously, go and win.

1360
01:03:21,464 --> 01:03:24,134
-I really hope you win.
-Had I known you'd do this,

1361
01:03:24,718 --> 01:03:25,969
I wouldn't have talked to you.

1362
01:03:30,015 --> 01:03:31,016
-[Pani Bottle] I...
-Let's go.

1363
01:03:31,099 --> 01:03:34,561
-[Pani Bottle] I didn't vote for you.
-[Dail] Let's go. I picked you.

1364
01:03:34,644 --> 01:03:36,563
-[Pani Bottle] Because I told you to.
-I picked you.

1365
01:03:36,646 --> 01:03:38,565
ELIMINATION CANDIDATES
PANI BOTTLE, YANG DAIL

1366
01:03:42,569 --> 01:03:44,571
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1367
01:03:46,031 --> 01:03:47,157
[Jieun] This is crazy.

1368
01:03:47,240 --> 01:03:49,117
[Jieun and Jaegyun laugh]

1369
01:03:49,993 --> 01:03:51,202
It's freezing.

1370
01:03:51,286 --> 01:03:52,871
THE SURVIVORS ARRIVE AT THE LODGING

1371
01:03:53,455 --> 01:03:56,374
-[ZZONE gasps]
-Isn't that a pool?

1372
01:03:57,375 --> 01:03:58,376
[gasps]

1373
01:03:59,419 --> 01:04:01,963
-[Joonsu] You want to jump straight in?
-Can we go in there?

1374
01:04:02,964 --> 01:04:05,425
[Jieun] This is crazy.
Is this where food is?

1375
01:04:05,508 --> 01:04:08,053
-[Jimin] This is insane.
-[Jieun] I'm hungry. I see ramyeon.

1376
01:04:08,136 --> 01:04:09,137
DINING ROOM

1377
01:04:12,432 --> 01:04:14,142
[Jimin] This must be the Main Hall.

1378
01:04:14,225 --> 01:04:15,226
MAIN HALL

1379
01:04:15,810 --> 01:04:17,395
VOTING ROOM

1380
01:04:17,479 --> 01:04:19,189
ROOM 1 ON FIRST FLOOR

1381
01:04:19,272 --> 01:04:20,899
ROOM 2 ON FIRST FLOOR

1382
01:04:20,982 --> 01:04:22,567
ROOM ON SECOND FLOOR,

1383
01:04:22,650 --> 01:04:26,446
When I saw the house,
it felt like, "I've survived."

1384
01:04:26,529 --> 01:04:30,158
But knowing this could end up
being my grave,

1385
01:04:30,241 --> 01:04:32,619
I wasn't sure how I should've felt.

1386
01:04:32,702 --> 01:04:35,121
We'll take the second floor
since we're younger.

1387
01:04:35,205 --> 01:04:38,249
-I think the rooms might have an effect.
-Right.

1388
01:04:39,334 --> 01:04:40,794
[Horseking] This feels strange.

1389
01:04:41,419 --> 01:04:45,507
ALL SURVIVING PLAYERS HAVE CHECKED IN

1390
01:04:47,759 --> 01:04:49,594
[Dail] Geez, from the first day...

1391
01:04:50,845 --> 01:04:51,846
Fucking hell.

1392
01:04:52,847 --> 01:04:54,849
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1393
01:04:55,725 --> 01:04:57,143
What's this?

1394
01:04:59,938 --> 01:05:00,939
[exclaims]

1395
01:05:01,981 --> 01:05:04,025
[chuckles]

1396
01:05:10,406 --> 01:05:13,326
PRISON

1397
01:05:14,160 --> 01:05:16,788
-She's been here all along.
-[Pani Bottle] Gyeong Sujin?

1398
01:05:21,709 --> 01:05:23,837
A FEW HOURS AGO

1399
01:05:23,920 --> 01:05:26,256
[Sujin] I knew this would happen. [sighs]

1400
01:05:26,339 --> 01:05:27,715
What is this?

1401
01:05:28,842 --> 01:05:29,843
Am I a prisoner?

1402
01:05:30,718 --> 01:05:32,178
You've got to be kidding me.

1403
01:05:32,262 --> 01:05:34,222
[Sujin] I really have to wear
a prison uniform?

1404
01:05:34,305 --> 01:05:35,849
It actually made me...

1405
01:05:37,058 --> 01:05:38,268
more determined.

1406
01:05:39,727 --> 01:05:41,062
I thought...

1407
01:05:41,646 --> 01:05:43,565
"Just you wait and see how I get out."

1408
01:05:43,648 --> 01:05:44,649
Just watch.

1409
01:05:46,025 --> 01:05:47,652
So I made sure to eat well...

1410
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:50,155
and build up my strength.

1411
01:05:51,823 --> 01:05:54,826
SUJIN WAS MOTIVATED BUT THEN GOT DRAINED

1412
01:05:54,909 --> 01:05:56,244
[Dail] This is going to be fun.

1413
01:05:56,327 --> 01:05:57,829
THE ELIMINATION CANDIDATES MEET IN PRISON

1414
01:05:57,912 --> 01:05:59,038
[Pani Bottle] This is great.

1415
01:06:00,331 --> 01:06:01,624
[mic feedback]

1416
01:06:01,708 --> 01:06:04,460
[host] Everyone,
please gather in the Main Hall.

1417
01:06:04,544 --> 01:06:06,588
-[Eunsil] Hello.
-[Jieun] Hi.

1418
01:06:06,671 --> 01:06:07,797
-You're looking good.
-What?

1419
01:06:07,881 --> 01:06:09,799
-You look happy.
-I slept well.

1420
01:06:09,883 --> 01:06:10,884
[Jaegyun] No wonder.

1421
01:06:10,967 --> 01:06:12,635
[mic feedback]

1422
01:06:12,719 --> 01:06:16,306
[host] Congratulations to everyone
who survived the first Main Match.

1423
01:06:16,848 --> 01:06:20,727
We will now begin the first Seeker Vote.

1424
01:06:20,810 --> 01:06:21,811
What?

1425
01:06:22,478 --> 01:06:23,980
-Seeker?
-[Jieun] What?

1426
01:06:24,063 --> 01:06:25,565
-Seeker Vote?
-[Jieun] What?

1427
01:06:26,816 --> 01:06:29,235
[Horseking] It turns out
there's a Seeker. [gasps]

1428
01:06:29,319 --> 01:06:30,612
[Eunsil] What's going on?

1429
01:06:31,613 --> 01:06:33,823
[host] The Seeker is a hidden architect

1430
01:06:33,907 --> 01:06:36,326
who creates chaos and controls
the course of the chase,

1431
01:06:36,409 --> 01:06:39,579
secretly working
to prevent the players from winning.

1432
01:06:40,455 --> 01:06:41,664
[exhales]

1433
01:06:42,749 --> 01:06:45,293
[Jieun gasps] Damn, this is insane.

1434
01:06:46,920 --> 01:06:49,797
[Sanghyun] There's a Seeker here
all of a sudden?

1435
01:06:50,965 --> 01:06:51,966
[sighs]

1436
01:06:53,635 --> 01:06:56,763
[Jaegyun] I couldn't process it
for a moment.

1437
01:06:56,846 --> 01:06:59,641
[Horseking] We were fooled.
They played us from the start.

1438
01:06:59,724 --> 01:07:02,143
I don't know. I can't trust anything.

1439
01:07:02,227 --> 01:07:04,812
Yeah, it's boring to just play games.

1440
01:07:06,022 --> 01:07:08,566
[Jimin] This is going to be
really interesting.

1441
01:07:09,067 --> 01:07:11,110
Someone has been fooling us.

1442
01:07:13,363 --> 01:07:17,951
LAST NIGHT, WHILE EVERYONE WAS ASLEEP

1443
01:07:22,080 --> 01:07:25,792
SOMEONE WAS MOVING IN SECRET

1444
01:07:29,045 --> 01:07:31,214
[host] The Seeker Room has opened.

1445
01:07:36,052 --> 01:07:37,053
DEADLY TAG
RULES

1446
01:07:37,136 --> 01:07:40,098
[dealer] Seeker [bleep],
select a player for elimination.

1447
01:07:41,599 --> 01:07:43,851
[distorted voice 1]
It was really thrilling.

1448
01:07:43,935 --> 01:07:46,521
[distorted voice 2] If you stand out,
you'll get eliminated fast.

1449
01:07:50,108 --> 01:07:52,360
[host] We will begin the Seeker Vote.

1450
01:07:52,443 --> 01:07:53,528
[Jimin] What's going on?

1451
01:07:53,611 --> 01:07:55,113
[Horseking] It turns out there's a Seeker.

1452
01:07:55,196 --> 01:07:57,365
[Jaegyun] Someone has been fooling us.

1453
01:07:57,448 --> 01:08:00,743
[Dail] You can't trust these damn people.

1454
01:08:00,827 --> 01:08:03,079
[♪ dramatic music playing]

1455
01:08:03,663 --> 01:08:04,664
[Jieun] Are you the Seeker?

1456
01:08:04,747 --> 01:08:07,292
[Jaegyun] The Seeker's doing
something here right now.

1457
01:08:07,375 --> 01:08:09,502
[Jimin] They create chaos
and control how the game goes.

1458
01:08:09,585 --> 01:08:11,254
[Jieun] This is all the Seeker's doing?

1459
01:08:11,337 --> 01:08:14,173
[Pani Bottle] I was going crazy.
That God damn ridiculous Seeker.

1460
01:08:14,257 --> 01:08:16,926
[Horseking]
The Seeker's playing us right now.

1461
01:08:17,010 --> 01:08:18,094
I'm so pissed off.

1462
01:08:18,177 --> 01:08:19,304
[Pani Bottle] Fuck!

1463
01:08:20,972 --> 01:08:22,348
[Jimin] Shit, who is it?

1464
01:08:23,141 --> 01:08:24,976
[Seeker] Can you find me?

1465
01:08:25,059 --> 01:08:27,270
Catch me if you can.

1466
01:08:27,353 --> 01:08:29,063
[Junseo] Catch them!

1467
01:08:29,564 --> 01:08:30,940
[Pani Bottle] Do it now!

1468
01:08:31,024 --> 01:08:32,442
-It's okay! Go!
-[ZZONE] When did it switch?

1469
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:34,110
I never did that.
What are you talking about?

1470
01:08:34,193 --> 01:08:35,528
[ZZONE] Hang on!

1471
01:08:35,611 --> 01:08:38,072
What's with you?
It's just us. Why can't you talk?

1472
01:08:38,156 --> 01:08:40,241
If you confuse me,
I'll accuse you of being the Seeker.

1473
01:08:40,325 --> 01:08:41,993
We could've eliminated them, so why...

1474
01:08:42,076 --> 01:08:44,370
[Jimin] Let's eliminate the strongest one.

1475
01:08:44,454 --> 01:08:46,164
[Jieun] I didn't want
to get eliminated first.

1476
01:08:46,247 --> 01:08:47,790
[Jimin] It'll be fucking hard
to play together.

1477
01:08:47,874 --> 01:08:50,084
[Pani Bottle groans]
I should rip out all that pink hair.

1478
01:08:50,168 --> 01:08:52,712
[Sujin] Did I really do
something that bad?

1479
01:08:52,795 --> 01:08:54,130
[sobbing]

1480
01:08:54,630 --> 01:08:55,965
[Pani Bottle] This game fucking sucks.

1481
01:08:56,799 --> 01:08:59,344
[Seeker] I guess you'll have to go. Bye.

1482
01:09:00,011 --> 01:09:01,929
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1483
01:09:21,949 --> 01:09:23,951
Translated by Youji Kim
